var e={"09-05":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY PROPHET ZACHARIAS THE FATHER OF THE HONORABLE FORERUNNER JOHN THE BAPTIST`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 5th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`six_stichera`,fekula_section:`2C`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`09-05.pdf`,note:'OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). First FILE of 5 September; the second, 09-05A, is a Polyeleos service of the Prophet Zacharias and Righteous Elizabeth and is the one V1 encoded and ODS 3rd ed. vol. III (pp. 14-16, `ods3-0905-wkd`) follows. This file is the lesser form: by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, 6 stichera of one saint (three printed, each "(Twice)"), a Glory of the saint, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology: Six-Stichera, Fekula 2C. `oca_primary` is false because the vol. III entry and V1 take the second service. Two files are two services (ruling of 14 Nov 2026). The aposticha print only their Glory and Both now at Vespers and at Matins ("At the Stichera, Glory ...").',troparion:{text:`Arrayed in the vesture of the priesthood, * and in accordance with the law, * thou didst offer the sacrifice of oblation in a sacred manner O all-wise one, * and wast manifestly a beacon and seer of sacred mysteries, * who bore within thyself the tokens of grace, * and thou wast slain by the sword in the Temple of God O prophet of Christ, ** together with the forerunner entreat Him that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy prophet, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Today Zacharias, the prophet and high priest of the Most High, * the father of the Forerunner, * setteth the table of his memorial, * feeding the faithful; * for he hath distributed the food of righteousness unto all. * Wherefore, he hath reposed * as a divine initiate ** of the mysteries of the grace of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:3},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},ikos:{text:`The high priest of the law was bound to silence by the voice of an angel, for within the barren and chaste Elizabeth, the angel of the coming of Christ, the prophet and initiate of the mysteries was to come forth. By his nativity, the grace, deliverance, universal reconciliation and renewal of our nature was to be revealed. By Him Who giveth fruit from the barren womb, the Son Who hath appeared from the Virgin, the divine initiate of the mysteries of the grace of God and his preaching of the Lamb was to be made manifest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer_rubric`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” we chant 6 Stichera of the holy prophet, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`With the oil of anointing and holy vesture upon thyself, * O ever-memorable Zacharias, * thou didst minister unto God like an angel, * mediating, O blessed one, * between the Creator and His creation, * and manifestly receiving the words of the divine Spirit. * Wherefore, we call thee blessed, * and celebrate today thy holy festival, ** glorifying the Savior.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`},{text:`O divinely inspired Zacharias, * thou didst behold born of a maiden * a Babe Who is co-beginningless with the Father; * and unto thine own child thou dost prophecy manifestly beforehand: * “A prophet shalt thou truly be, * preparing His ways!” * With him we call thee blessed * and in a sacred manner we celebrate thine honored festival, ** O most noetically rich God-bearer.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`},{text:`Thou wast the living and animate temple * of the divine Spirit; * and, ministering unto God * with a pure heart, O glorious one, * in the midst of the temple thou wast unjustly slain, * finishing thy godly course in martyrdom, O right-glorious one. * Wherefore, with thine own blood * thou hast entered into the temple of heaven, ** entreating cleansing for our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Truly arrayed in the vestments of the priesthood of the law, thou didst serve according to the order of Aaron; and, standing in the temple, thou didst clearly behold the countenance of the angel, O most blessed one. Wherefore, hymning thy repose as is meet, O Zacharias, we all praise with songs thee who, in thine old age, begat the glorious John. Entreat thou the merciful God for us, that we be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},composer:`John the Monk`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of John the Monk, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., the Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`“What is this sight which I see, * which mine eyes behold, O Master? * How is it that Thou Who dost sustain all creation, * art lifted up upon the Tree and diest, * granting life unto all? * thus said the Theotokos weeping, * upon seeing God and man * Who had shone forth ineffably from her ** hanging upon the Cross.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:8,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},aposticha_glory:{text:`As a pure priest thou didst enter into the holy of holies and, clad in sacred vesture, didst blamelessly minister unto God, observing the law like Aaron and leading the tribes of Israel like Moses, in the pure signaling of the little bells. Wherefore, thou wast slain. But thy righteous blood hath become for us a saving healing, and like fragrant myrrh it openeth deaf ears to the way of everlasting life. O thrice blessed Zacharias, father of John the Baptist and husband of Elizabeth: pray thou earnestly on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p1-p2 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`On the Aposticha, Glory ..., in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`When the unblemished ewe-lamb beheld her Lamb * willingly led as a man to the slaughter, * she said, weeping: * “Dost Thou now hasten to leave me childless * who gave Thee birth O Christ,? * What is this that Thou hast done, O Redeemer of all? * Even so I will hymn and glorify Thine extreme goodness, * which is beyond understanding and all telling, ** O Lover of mankind!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`When from the tree ...`},troparion_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion Theotokion rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without the martyria, and the canon of the holy prophet, with 6 Troparia; the composition of Theophanes in Tone I.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without the martyria, and the canon of the holy prophet, with 6 Troparia; the composition of Theophanes in Tone I.`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Having passed through the water as upon dry land, * and having escaped the malice of the Egyptians, * the Israelites cried aloud: * Unto our God and Redeemer let us sing.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`By thy mediation, O prophet, impart unto me the grace of the Spirit, to help me praise thy memory, crying out: Let us chant unto our Redeemer and God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy life was found to be blameless, and thou wast arrayed in the vesture of the priesthood and the luminous splendors of prophecy, O divinely eloquent and blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having thy head adorned with the crown of the law, O Zacharias, thou wast shown to be sacred, crying aloud: Let us chant unto our Redeemer and God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Clad in the vestment of the full-length tunic like Aaron, thou didst receive the maiden who sprouted forth from the root of Jesse and bore the Redeemer in her womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, thou art the confirmation of those who flee to Thee, * Thou art the Light of those in darkness, * and my spirit doth hymn Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When thou didst offer the incense of the covenant, O high priest, then didst thou receive the prophetic proclamation of the Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The priesthood anointed thee with oil to serve as a priest, like Aaron. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to behold the angel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias begat John, the dawn which announced to the whole world Thee, the noetic Sun, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Set my life aright, O all-pure Birthgiver of God, thou life which filled with light the house of Zacharias.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation; * I have considered Thy works, * and I have glorified Thy Divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy prophet, O Master, faithfully ministered unto Thee with the symbols of the law and was deemed worthy of the grace to perceive Thy truth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou, the most brilliant and most blessed one, didst receive light through darkest light; for through the law grace hath now been added unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The divine Gabriel, who standeth before God, announced and revealed to thee the manifestation of the voice and Forerunner of the Word, O blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Fashioner of creation, Who loosed the barrenness of Elizabeth, found thee, O Virgin, to be a pure habitation, and dwelt therein.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Rising early we cry to Thee, O Lord; * save us, for Thou art our God, * and we know none other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Upon thy head, O prophet, was the mitre placed which bore the impress of the true and divine priesthood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Creation rejoiceth in thine offspring, O high priest; for thou didst beget the preacher of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst lead a life adorned, for with Elizabeth thou didst keep all the commandments of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy tongue is directed toward hymnody, O divinely eloquent one; for thou didst behold her who knoweth not wedlock bearing a Child within her womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`O Thou that puttest on light as a garment * grant me also a robe of light, * O All-merciful Christ, our God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He who served the shadow of the law was shown to be a preacher of grace, O our Savior; for he was deemed worthy to behold Thine incarnation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adorned with words of judgment, O sacred Zacharias, thou didst receive the ever-existing Word bearing flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast shown to serve God in the temple as a right wondrous priest, O divinely inspired initiate of the mysteries of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast recognized by the prophetess Elizabeth, O Virgin Mother of God, bearing the beginningless Word and Savior in thy womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The Hebrew children in the furnace * boldly trampled upon the flames, * changing the fire into dew, they cried aloud: * ‘Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages’.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When the voice of one crying in the wilderness came forth from the barren woman supra-naturally, he loosed the bonds of thy tongue that thou couldst cry: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Forerunner, the beloved friend of the Bridegroom, was born of a barren woman, manifestly proclaiming the birthgiving of the Virgin unto those who cry out with faith: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thrice-blessed Zacharias, thou wast wholly a divine instrument of the Spirit, and didst proclaim thy son to be a prophet, who crieth: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias, beholding thee, recognized thee as the fulfillment of the law, the chief object of all prophecy, O maiden, and he cried aloud: Blessed is the fruit of thy womb, O most pure one!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Glorified in the holy mountain, * the Lord revealed the mystery of the ever-virgin unto Moses * in the flames of the burning bush: * praise ye and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast shown to be a prophet of the truth, for thou didst prepare John the Forerunner to tread first the paths of Christ, O blessed high priest. Him do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving voice in speech, thou didst bless the Master, the Lord of glory Who hath bestowed salvation upon us, Who shone forth upon us in the flesh from David. Him do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou was deemed worthy of great gifts, O divinely revealed one, begetting the Forerunner, the greatest of all the prophets, who hymneth and supremely exalteth the Lord throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing, Zacharias, the high priest and preacher of God, paid homage to the Virgin and Mother who beareth the Lord of creation. Her do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Saved by thee, O pure Virgin, * we confess thee to be truly the Theotokos, * and together with the choirs of the bodiless hosts * thee do we magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast filled with the inspiration of the Comforter and wast the beginning of the blessing of the Lord, O divinely wise initiate of the sacred mysteries, divinely blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Perceiving the fulfillment of the archangel’s words, O all-famed and divinely eloquent one, thou didst straightway move thy tongue to blessing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast adorned with crowns of suffering and the priesthood and with the enlightenment of prophecy, O most blessed Zacharias, divinely eloquent one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art the dwelling-place of the Light, O Virgin, illumine my soul which hath been darkened by the passions, and by thy supplications deliver me from the outermost darkness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having ministered to God as a priest according to the law, O Zacharias, thou wast shown to the whole world as a pillar of light, prophesying that Christ would come forth from the Virgin, incarnate of the Holy Spirit, the Orient from the heights of righteousness, Who doth illumine all the world, direct our feet to the ways of peace, and save our race, thou didst say.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy prophet, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`That which hath been commanded ...`,tone:8},{text:`O thou who hast given birth to the immutable God, * by thy maternal supplications * make steadfast my heart which is ever-changing due to sin, * slothfulness and the attacks of the deceiver; * that in thanksgiving I also may glorify thee O good one. * O all-immaculate Mary, Birthgiver of God, * have mercy on the flock ** which thou hast acquired.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Ever protected by the Cross of thy Son and God, O Virgin, we vanquish the assaults and wiles of the demons, hymning thee who art truly the Theotokos; and all generations bless thee with love, O most pure one, as thou didst foretell. Wherefore, by thy supplications grant us forgiveness of sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`At first, thou wast struck mute in the holy of holies, by the voice of the angel, for the springing forth from thee of the voice of one crying in the wilderness; and now thou art silent for his sake, slain, O Zacharias, before the holy of holies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy prophet`,spec_mel:`O Light immutable ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Having shone forth eternally, Light from Light, before the morning star, O Word, Thou didst come forth as Light, immutably, under time, from Thy Mother, illumining the ends of the world with radiant effulgence, as Thou art the Light of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},aposticha_glory:{text:`Offering sacrifices in accordance with the law, O Zacharias, thou didst willingly present thy holy soul to God, Who wast born in the flesh, as a whole-burnt offering in the Holy of Holies, when thou wast slain like a lamb by the sword, between the temple and the alter.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Matins Stichera, Glory`},sourceLabel:`At the Stichera, Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Stichera, Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`O Lord, when the sun beheld Thee * the Sun of righteousness, hanging upon the Tree, * it hid its rays, and the light of the moon was changed to darkness; * and Thine all-immaculate Mother ** was pierced in the depths of her soul.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Stichera Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:8,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`O Lord, before the tribunal ...`}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from the Oktoechos, and 4, from ODE III of the canon of the holy prophet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`When thou didst offer the incense of the covenant, O high priest, then didst thou receive the prophetic proclamation of the Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The priesthood anointed thee with oil to serve as a priest, like Aaron. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to behold the angel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias begat John, the dawn which announced to the whole world Thee, the noetic Sun, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Set my life aright, O all-pure Birthgiver of God, thou life which filled with light the house of Zacharias.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`The righteous man shall be glad in the Lord, * and shall hope in Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O God, unto my prayer, when I make supplication unto Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE HEBREWS,`,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§314 (HEB.6: 13-20)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:6,verses:`13-20`,pericope_number:314},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`A light hath dawned for the righteous man, and gladness for the upright of heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. MATTHEW,`,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 96 (MT. 23: 29-39)`,citation:{book:`Matthew`,chapter:23,verses:`29-39`,pericope_number:96},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}},{kind:`saint`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY PROPHET ZACHARIAS & THE HOLY & RIGHTEOUS ELIZABETH, THE PARENTS OF THE HONORABLE FORERUNNER JOHN THE BAPTIST`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 5th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`polyeleos`,fekula_section:`2E`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`09-05A.pdf`,note:`OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). Second FILE of 5 September and the service of the day: RANK IS PRINTED by ODS 3rd ed. vol. III, pp. 14-16, entry \`ods3-0905-wkd\` (a polyeleos-rank service on a weekday; encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 step 0), as V1 recorded. The page prints a Litiya ("the Sticheron of the temple, followed by these Stichera") in a Polyeleos service: the case vol. III allows for. 8 stichera, 4 of the prophet (three printed, the first "(Twice)") and 4 of the righteous Elizabeth (three printed, the first "(Twice)" on a line of its own). TWO canons, the prophet's (Theophanes, headed Tone VIII here; 09-05.pdf heads the same canon "Tone I") and the righteous one's, interleaved, stored whole. One troparion "of the righteous ones" (entry-level); two kontakia, one per saint, in positional lists. The three lessons print no reference; citations are V1's identifications. Ode I of the second canon ends with the katavasia as an incipit.`,troparion:{text:`Celebrating the memory of Thy righteous ones, * Zacharias and Elizabeth, O Lord, * through them do we entreat Thee: ** Save Thou our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Troparion of the righteous ones`},saint:`Zacharias and Elizabeth`,verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 end of Vespers`,tone:2},{locus:`p18 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the righteous ones, in Tone II`,tone:2},vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`dogmatikon`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya`,`litiya_glory`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`],rubric:{text:`We chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera: 4 of the holy prophet, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`With the oil of anointing and holy vesture upon thyself, * O ever-memorable Zacharias, * thou didst minister unto God like an angel, * mediating, O blessed one, * between the Creator and His creation, * and manifestly receiving the words of the divine Spirit. * Wherefore, we call thee blessed, * and celebrate today thy holy festival, ** glorifying the Savior.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,tone:4,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`},{text:`O divinely inspired Zacharias, * thou didst behold born of a maiden * a Babe Who is co-beginningless with the Father; * and unto thine own child thou dost prophecy manifestly beforehand: * “A prophet shalt thou truly be, * preparing His ways!” * With him we call thee blessed * and in a sacred manner we celebrate thine honored festival, ** O most noetically rich God-bearer.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`},{text:`Thou wast the living and animate temple * of the divine Spirit; * and, ministering unto God * with a pure heart, O glorious one, * in the midst of the temple thou wast unjustly slain, * finishing thy godly course in martyrdom, O right-glorious one. * Wherefore, with thine own blood * thou hast entered into the temple of heaven, ** entreating cleansing for our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,spec_mel:`Thou hast granted a sign ...`},{text:`When thou didst call the Virgin who greeted thee * the Mother of thy Lord, * thou didst behold in her virginal womb * Him, incarnate, Whose goings forth are from before time began. * Pray with her, O righteous Elizabeth, ** that He save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`And 4 Stichera of the righteous Elizabeth, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`,tone:1},{text:`“Blessed is the Fruit of the Virgin’s womb, * Who filleth all things!”, * thou didst exclaim, O most blessed Elizabeth, * moved thus to speak by the Spirit of God. * Wherefore, honoring thee in hymns, ** we magnify God Who is worshiped in Trinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`That which was said by the Lord * became reality in the Virgin, * for she gave birth to Jesus Who saveth His people from their sins. * “He shall be the fulfillment of those things which were said to her,” * thou didst exclaim, inspired by the Holy Spirit, O Elizabeth. ** Wherefore, we crown thee with wreaths of praise, as is meet.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Truly arrayed in the vestments of the priesthood of the law, thou didst serve according to the order of Aaron; and, standing in the temple, thou didst clearly behold the countenance of the angel, O most blessed one. Wherefore, hymning thy repose as is meet, O Zacharias, we all praise with songs thee who, in thine old age, begat the glorious John. Entreat thou the merciful God for us, that we be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory`},composer:`John the Monk`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of John the Monk, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},dogmatikon:{text:`In His love for mankind, the King of heaven appeared on earth * and dwelt among men; * for He Who received flesh from the pure Virgin * and cameth forth from her having received human nature, * is the only Son of God, * twofold in nature but not Hypostasis. * Therefore, proclaiming Him to be truly perfect God and perfect man, * we confess Christ our God. * Him do thou beseech, O unwedded Mother, ** that our souls find mercy!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Both now, Dogmatic Theotokion`},type:`dogmatic_theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., the Dogmatic Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM GENESIS`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Genesis`,chapter:18,verses:`1-14`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "God appeared to Abraham by the oak of Mamre". No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file (identified from the printed text, not read off a printed reference); confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE BOOK OF JUDGES`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Judges`,chapter:13,verses:`2-20`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "And there was a man of Zorah" (the birth of Samson announced). No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file (identified from the printed text, not read off a printed reference); confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE FIRST BOOK OF KINGS`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`1 Kings`,chapter:1,verses:`9-20`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "And Hannah rose up after they had eaten in Shiloh" (First Kings, i.e. 1 Samuel). No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file (identified from the printed text, not read off a printed reference); confirm the span against the page.`}],litiya:[{text:`Seeing Jesus, John cried aloud: “Behold the Lamb of God!” fulfilling the prophecy of Isaiah. Thy son was the last of the prophets, O Elizabeth. Wherefore, the people call thee blessed, as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`At Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple, followed by these Stichera, in Tone VI`,tone:6},{text:`Jesus, Who is the Lord of lords and Master of masters, bowed His head beneath the right hand of thy son. Great is thy glory, O right-laudable Elizabeth!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The voice of one crying in the wilderness denounced the boastful Pharisees, saying unto them: “O generation of vipers, bring forth fruits worthy of repentance!” And he worshiped the Master. Of such a son art thou the mother, O holy Elizabeth!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya 3`},label:`plain`}],litiya_glory:{text:`Keeping the commandments of God, thou didst bring forth the fruit of living faith which dwelt within thee, O divinely wise Elizabeth. With what worthy hymns, with what worthy praises can we, the faithful, crown thee?`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},litiya_closer:{text:`Christ the Lord, my Creator and Redeemer, * Who came forth from thy womb, O most pure one, * and clothed Himself in my nature, * hath freed Adam from the primal curse. * Wherefore, like the angel * we unceasingly cry out to thee, * O all-pure one, * who art truly the Mother of God and Virgin: * Rejoice!, O Sovereign Lady, ** the intercession, protection and salvation of our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the righteous one, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Thou art worthy of many praises, O divinely wise Elizabeth, who art called righteous by the word of God, thou didst walk blamelessly in the commandments of the Lord, moved so by the mercy of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,saint:`Elizabeth`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Walking in the commandments of the Lord, O abundantly glorious Elizabeth, thou didst have unfeigned love for God and unfeigned love for thy neighbor. And, lo! the fruit of thy faith was made reality. Wherefore, holding festival, we call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`},{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord; * in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`A most glorious fruit of the womb was given by the most compassionate God to thee, a woman barren and past childbearing: the preacher of repentance. Wherefore, calling thee blessed, we magnify the almighty mercy of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`As a pure priest thou didst enter into the holy of holies and, clad in sacred vesture, blamelessly ministered unto God, observing the law like Aaron and leading the tribes of Israel like Moses, in the pure signaling of the little bells. Wherefore, thou wast slain. But thy righteous blood hath become for us a salvific healing, like fragrant myrrh opening the ears of the deaf leading them to the way of everlasting life. O thrice blessed Zacharias, father of John the Baptist and husband of Elizabeth: pray thou earnestly on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha Glory, of the holy prophet`},composer:`Anatolius`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., of the holy prophet, the composition of Anatolius, in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_closer:{text:`O new wonder greater than all the wonders of old! * For who hath ever known a mother to give birth without having known a man, * and to bear on her arm Him Who sustaineth all creation? * Yet it was the will of God to be born. * O most pure one, who carried Him as an infant in Thine embrace * and before Whom thou hast a mother’s boldness: * cease not to pray on behalf of those who honor thee, ** that He have compassion and save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2},troparion_closer:{text:`All of thy most glorious mysteries are beyond comprehension, * O Theotokos; * for, thy purity sealed and thy virginity intact, * thou art known to be a true Mother, having given birth unto God. ** Him do thou entreat, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Troparion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2}},matins:{order:`sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.kontakia_ode3.sessional_ode3.kontakia_ode6.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_glory.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric`.split(`.`),sessional_1:[{text:`Great is the love for mankind which the supremely good God hath toward mortals, and which He showed thee, O Elizabeth, in that it was His will, in His ineffable goodness, that thou be with Zacharias. What thanksgiving is due to Thee, O Merciful One! What hymns can we, Thy sinful servants, offer to Thee, O Master?`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Through the overshadowing of the Holy Spirit, Who cameth from on high, O all-immaculate one, thou didst conceive and bear Him Who existed from before all ages. Let creation hold festival, praising thee and magnifying thy most glorious birthgiving; and let her who hath borne the Redeemer of our souls, the only blessed one, chant, made glad by spiritual joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],sessional_2:[{text:`Samuel was a most welcome gift to the barren Hannah, and unto thee, O righteous Elizabeth, was the namesake of grace bestowed most joyously. Wondrous is Thy mercy unto mankind, O God! Glory to Thy many compassions! Glory to Thy loving-kindness!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`O Mother who hast not known wedlock, thy womb hath been shown to be the cherubic throne of the unapproachable God; for thou alone art the dwelling-place of God, having given birth unto God incarnate Who delivereth His servants from all sins. Wherefore, meet it is to call thee blessed with heart and lips.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this Megalynarion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 megalynarion rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify you, O holy and righteous Zacharias and Elizabeth, and we honor your holy memory; for ye entreat Christ our God on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Megalynarion`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm Verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Selected Psalm Verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Blessed be the Lord God of Israel; for He hath visited and wrought redemption for His people.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God! (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`Blossoming forth in the statutes of God with the most blessed Zacharias, O all-praised Elizabeth, offshoot of the daughters of Aaron, thou wast moved by the hand of God. Entreat the supremely good Master that we sinners may also offer the good fruit of living faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Thou alone art the Mother of God, thou alone art ever-virgin. O most pure Bride of God, in that thou hast given birth as a virgin, and remainest incorrupt. Wherefore, the ranks of angels and men magnify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],prokeimenon:{text:`In the saints that are in His earth hath the Lord been wondrous; * He hath wrought all His desires in them.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE.`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 2 (LK. 1: 5-25)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:1,verses:`5-25`,pericope_number:2},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`That which was said by the Lord became reality in the Virgin, for she gave birth to Jesus Who saveth His people from their sins. “He shall be the fulfillment of those things which were said to her,” thou didst exclaim, inspired by the Holy Spirit, O Elizabeth. Wherefore, we crown thee with wreaths of praise, as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone I`,tone:1},canon_rubric:{text:`Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia, including its Irmos; canon of the holy prophet, with 4 Troparia; and canon of the righteous one, with 4 Troparia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the prophet Zacharias, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone VIII:`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Having passed through the water as upon dry land, * and having escaped the malice of the Egyptians, * the Israelites cried aloud: * Unto our God and Redeemer let us sing.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`By thy mediation, O prophet, impart unto me the grace of the Spirit, to help me praise thy memory, crying out: Let us chant unto our Redeemer and God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy life was found to be blameless, and thou wast arrayed in the vesture of the priesthood and the luminous splendors of prophecy, O divinely eloquent and blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having thy head adorned with the crown of the law, O Zacharias, thou wast shown to be sacred, crying aloud: Let us chant unto our Redeemer and God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Clad in the vestment of the full-length tunic like Aaron, thou didst receive the maiden who sprouted forth from the root of Jesse and bore the Redeemer in her womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, thou art the confirmation of those who flee to Thee, * Thou art the Light of those in darkness, * and my spirit doth hymn Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When thou didst offer the incense of the covenant, O high priest, then didst thou receive the prophetic proclamation of the Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The priesthood anointed thee with oil to serve as a priest, like Aaron. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to behold the angel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias begat John, the dawn which announced to the whole world Thee, the noetic Sun, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Set my life aright, O all-pure Birthgiver of God, thou life which filled with light the house of Zacharias.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation; * I have considered Thy works, * and I have glorified Thy Divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy prophet, O Master, faithfully ministered unto Thee with the symbols of the law and was deemed worthy of the grace to perceive Thy truth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou, the most brilliant and most blessed one, didst receive light through darkest light; for through the law grace hath now been added unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The divine Gabriel, who standeth before God, announced and revealed to thee the manifestation of the voice and Forerunner of the Word, O blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Fashioner of creation, Who loosed the barrenness of Elizabeth, found thee, O Virgin, to be a pure habitation, and dwelt therein.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Rising early we cry to Thee, O Lord; * save us, for Thou art our God, * and we know none other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Upon thy head, O prophet, was the mitre placed which bore the impress of the true and divine priesthood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Creation rejoiceth in thine offspring, O high priest; for thou didst beget the preacher of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst lead a life adorned, for with Elizabeth thou didst keep all the commandments of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy tongue is directed toward hymnody, O divinely eloquent one; for thou didst behold her who knoweth not wedlock bearing a Child within her womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`O Thou that puttest on light as a garment * grant me also a robe of light, * O All-merciful Christ, our God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He who served the shadow of the law was shown to be a preacher of grace, O our Savior; for he was deemed worthy to behold Thine incarnation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adorned with words of judgment, O sacred Zacharias, thou didst receive the ever-existing Word bearing flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast shown to serve God in the temple as a right wondrous priest, O divinely inspired initiate of the mysteries of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast recognized by the prophetess Elizabeth, O Virgin Mother of God, bearing the beginningless Word and Savior in thy womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The Hebrew children in the furnace * boldly trampled upon the flames, * changing the fire into dew, they cried aloud: * ‘Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages’.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When the voice of one crying in the wilderness came forth from the barren woman supra-naturally, he loosed the bonds of thy tongue that thou couldst cry: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Forerunner, the beloved friend of the Bridegroom, was born of a barren woman, manifestly proclaiming the birthgiving of the Virgin unto those who cry out with faith: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thrice-blessed Zacharias, thou wast wholly a divine instrument of the Spirit, and didst proclaim thy son to be a prophet, who crieth: Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias, beholding thee, recognized thee as the fulfillment of the law, the chief object of all prophecy, O maiden, and he cried aloud: Blessed is the fruit of thy womb, O most pure one!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Glorified in the holy mountain, * the Lord revealed the mystery of the ever-virgin unto Moses * in the flames of the burning bush: * praise ye and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast shown to be a prophet of the truth, for thou didst prepare John the Forerunner to tread first the paths of Christ, O blessed high priest. Him do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving voice in speech, thou didst bless the Master, the Lord of glory Who hath bestowed salvation upon us, Who shone forth upon us in the flesh from David. Him do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou was deemed worthy of great gifts, O divinely revealed one, begetting the Forerunner, the greatest of all the prophets, who hymneth and supremely exalteth the Lord throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing, Zacharias, the high priest and preacher of God, paid homage to the Virgin and Mother who beareth the Lord of creation. Her do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Saved by thee, O pure Virgin, * we confess thee to be truly the Theotokos, * and together with the choirs of the bodiless hosts * thee do we magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast filled with the inspiration of the Comforter and wast the beginning of the blessing of the Lord, O divinely wise initiate of the sacred mysteries, divinely blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Perceiving the fulfillment of the archangel’s words, O all-famed and divinely eloquent one, thou didst straightway move thy tongue to blessing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast adorned with crowns of suffering and the priesthood and with the enlightenment of prophecy, O most blessed Zacharias, divinely eloquent one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art the dwelling-place of the Light, O Virgin, illumine my soul which hath been darkened by the passions, and by thy supplications deliver me from the outermost darkness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}},{title:`Canon of the righteous one, in Tone VIII:`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`To Him who crushed the enemy with His arm * and led Israel through the Red Sea, * to our Redeemer and our God let us sing, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst have true love for God, O right loving Elizabeth, preserving His commandments; for those who keepeth His commandments truly love God. Wherefore, we magnify thee, beloved of God, with praises.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`We who are saved by grace must please God with virtues, just as Elizabeth walked in the commandments of the Lord blamelessly, whom let us bless with hymns, as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O God Who dost accomplish all things, Thou didst manifest Thine almighty mercy in the blessed Elizabeth. We offer thee thanks for all Thy works.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving birth to Isaac, Sarah rejoiced; and when thou, O Virgin, didst give birth to the Lord Jesus, it was fitting that thou rejoice yet more, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Tracing an upright line with his staff ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},3:{irmos:{text:`My heart is established in the Lord, * my horn is exalted in my God, * my mouth is enlarged against mine enemies, * and I rejoice in Thy salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`In the Scriptures, the Holy Spirit called thee and Zacharias righteous, O blessed Elizabeth, saying that ye were righteous in the sight of God. The Messiah is the truth for us from God, and therefore, by the Messiah wast thou justified. Who will not magnify thee with hymns of praise?`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Not everyone who liveth is justified in God’s sight; but in that thou wast righteous, O ever-memorable Elizabeth, the Lord Jesus sanctified thee. Let each of us praise thee as holy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O God Who art wondrous in Thy saints, Thou wast wondrous also in the blessed Elizabeth. We offer unto Thee, the most compassionate One, a hymn of thanksgiving.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The barren Sarah, giving birth in her old age, was blessed to be a mother. We are at a loss, O most pure one, how to praise thee, Mother and Virgin, as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`With noetic eyes the prophet Habbakuk * foresaw Thy coming, O Lord; * wherefore he cried aloud: * ‘God shall come out of Theman!’ Glory to Thy power! * Glory to Thy condescension!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As the wife of Zacharias, thou didst walk blamelessly in all the commandments; but there were others, virgins, who possessed not the oil of the virtues. Better is thy dignity than their virginity. Let people of every age glorify thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Paul, betrothing the faithful to Christ, referred to the betrothed as pure virgins saying: I have betrothed you a pure virgin to one Husband. How much more hath God joined to the wise virgins thee who hast walked in all His commandments, O divinely wise Elizabeth. Wherefore, we praise thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou, O God, hast shown the blessed Zacharias and Elizabeth, who walked in the commandments of the Lord, to be a model of how to please Thee, like unto the pillar of fire and the cloud when Israel was journeying to the promised land. Ineffable is Thy love for mankind, O almighty Master!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The birth of Isaac removed the reproach of childlessness from his mother and magnified her with glory; and when the Holy One was born of thee, O most pure Virgin and Mother, He brought thee pristine glory. Let every mortal glorify thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Lord our God, bestow Thy peace upon us; * O Lord our God, take us for Thy possession; * O Lord, besides Thee we know none other: * and we call upon Thy Name.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`To him whom God, through His angel, spake in the prophecy of Malachi, saying: “Behold, I will send Mine angel before Thy face”, didst thou, a barren woman, give birth, O Elizabeth. We crown thee with worthy praises.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The voice of God crying in the wilderness is born of thee, O most honored Elizabeth. Wherefore, who will not praise thee as the mouth of God?`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As once from a barren rock Thou didst pour forth water for Thy people, O God, so from the barren Elizabeth Thou hast given the preacher of repentance. O almighty Master, most glorious are all Thy works!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Two sons, Joseph and Benjamin, did the barren Rachel bring forth as fruit; and she is honored for her goodly offspring. And thou, a Virgin, hast given birth to Him Who is one in Hypostasis but dual in essence. Ineffable is thy glory, O Mother of Emmanuel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The billows of life trouble me like the waters of the sea, * O Lover of Mankind. * Wherefore, like Jonah I cry unto Thee, O Word: * Raise up my life from corruption, O compassionate Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When John was in thy womb, O holy Elizabeth, seeing His Savior he, the babe, did leap. Blessed is thy womb which made manifest the babe who recognized Jesus as his salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by the Holy Spirit against the will of others, O most blessed Elizabeth, thou didst name thy son John. Let everyone praise thee, the instrument of the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O God, Thou didst show forth Elizabeth’s conceiving as an image of Thine own inconceivable birthgiving from the Virgin. Glory to Thy mighty wisdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`When he was born of Rachel, Benjamin caused his own mother’s death; but the Word Who was born of thee is the true life of all. Him do thou beseech, that we who place our trust in Him may have everlasting life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Having quenched the all-consuming power of the Chaldean furnace * with the form of the angel, that had descended therein, * the children cried out to the Creator: * Blessed and praised art Thou, O God of our fathers!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O divinely wise Elizabeth, thou teachest us to give thanks unto God, saying of thy birthgiving: “Thus hath the Lord dealt with me!” And therein thou wast a teacher instructed by God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He whom the angel, within the sanctuary, told Zacharias to call John, thou didst thus name, instructed by God, when he was born of thee for all people. Thy tongue is like unto the angels’, O ever-memorable Elizabeth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As when God, making the heavens heavy with manna, let it fall upon His people in the wilderness, so hath He given us John, the herald of grace, through the blessed Elizabeth. Great is Thy mercy toward mankind, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving birth to Isaac, a prefiguring of Christ, Sarah said: “The Lord hath made me to laugh!” But do thou, O all-praised Mother and Virgin, who hast given birth to Him Whom Isaac prefigured and yet hast remained a Virgin, rejoice yet more.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O Thou who dost cover Thy chambers on high with waters, * Thou Who hast set the sands to bound the sea * and Who upholdest all things: * the sun doth sing Thy praises, * the moon giveth Thee glory, * every creature offereth a hymn unto Thee, * as their Fashioner, throughout the ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As God said of His Church: “Thou art most comely, my beloved, and there is no blemish in thee”, so art thou also blameless, O righteous Elizabeth. In that the Lord Jesus is the sanctification of His faithful, we magnify thee as most comely.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The people saw thee, who didst walk in all the commandments of the Lord, freely justified by the grace of God, O right blessed Elizabeth. Wherefore, it is meet to glorify the mercy of God in thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Elizabeth was the first to proclaim the mystery wrought in Thee, O Jesus, when she said: “Blessed is the Fruit of the Virgin’s womb, Who is our Lord and God!” Behold the working of Thy wisdom! Glory to Thy love for mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The birth of Samuel from his barren mother did away with the tears of her eyes and brought her joy; and the Lord born of thee is the cause of joy for the whole world. Wherefore we unceasingly magnify thee with hymns, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Virginity is alien to motherhood, * and childbearing is a thing strange to virgins: * yet in thee, O Theotokos, both have come to pass. * Therefore we, and all the nations of the earth, * without ceasing call thee blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Believing the Messiah Who had come to be thy Lord, and keeping the commandments of the Lord, thou didst well please Him, O Elizabeth. Wherefore, entreat the supremely good Master on behalf of those who bear thy name and all who praise thee, that their souls may be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He who keepeth the commandments of God hath God promised to love and appear to him; wherefore, thou art loved by God, O Elizabeth, who didst walk in His commandments. Entreat the supremely good One on behalf of those who bear thy name, that they may love God and be loved through His tender compassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Elizabeth, the kinswoman of Mary, hath given birth, though barren and bereft of children. Thou didst magnify Thy mercy with her, O God, for every good work cometh from Thee. Glory to Thine ineffable compassion!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sampson, was revealed to be strong from his youth, and was the glory of his barren mother. And in Jesus Who was born of thee hath all the fullness of the Godhead been embodied. We magnify thee, who art more glorious than all the saints, O most pure Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`Today Zacharias, the prophet and high priest of the Most High, * the father of the Forerunner, * setteth the table of his memorial, * feeding the faithful; * for he hath distributed the food of righteousness unto all. * Wherefore, he hath reposed * as a divine initiate ** of the mysteries of the grace of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Kontakion of the holy prophet (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},{text:`The high priest of the law was bound to silence by the voice of an angel, for within the barren and chaste Elizabeth, the angel of the coming of Christ, the prophet and initiate of the mysteries was to come forth. By his nativity, the grace, deliverance, universal reconciliation and renewal of our nature was to be revealed. By Him Who giveth fruit from the barren womb, the Son Who hath appeared from the Virgin, the divine initiate of the mysteries of the grace of God and his preaching of the Lamb was to be made manifest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p10-p11 Ikos of the holy prophet`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having ministered to God as a priest according to the law, O Zacharias, thou wast shown to the whole world as a pillar of light, prophesying that Christ would come forth from the Virgin, incarnate of the Holy Spirit, the Orient from the heights of righteousness, Who doth illumine all the world, direct our feet to the ways of peace, and save our race, thou didst say.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional (prophet)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy prophet, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`That which hath been commanded ...`,tone:8},{text:`When the Messiah was already incarnate, we listened to thee, His first herald, when, with awe, thou didst say unto the divinely chosen maiden who embraced thee: “Whence is this to me, that the Mother of my Lord should come to me?” Wherefore, praising thee, we cry aloud: Rejoice, thou mirror revealing the mysteries of God to us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional (righteous one)`},label:`glory`,saint:`Elizabeth`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Sessional Hymn of the righteous one, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`We, thy sinful servants, saved by thee through the Son Who was born of thee, confess thee to be our Sovereign Lady, O Theotokos; for having given birth inaccessibly unto God Who cleanseth us of every sin by His own blood and bringeth us into the joy of paradise, in gladness we praise thee and Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],kontakia_ode6:[{text:`Like the full moon, * thou didst receive the light of righteousness from the Messiah, * the noetic Sun, * O Elizabeth beloved of God, * and with Zacharias didst walk in all the commandments of the Lord. * Wherefore, blessing thee with worthy hymns, * we magnify the Lord, ** the most compassionate Light, Who illumineth all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Kontakion of the righteous one (after Ode VI)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the righteous one, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`As God once inscribed His commandments upon two tablets of stone, so hath He illumined you with His grace, O blessed Zacharias and Elizabeth; for ye walked blamelessly in His commandments. Therefore, worthily praising you, we magnify the Lord of all, the most compassionate Light Who illumineth all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ikos of the righteous one`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`At first, thou wast struck mute in the holy of holies, by the voice of the angel, for the springing forth from thee of the voice of one crying in the wilderness; and now thou art silent for his sake, slain, O Zacharias, before the holy of holies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Exapostilarion of the prophet`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the prophet`,spec_mel:`O Light immutable ...`},exapostilarion_glory:{text:`Thou wast the glory of barren mothers, the model of virtues for sinners, O blessed Elizabeth, keeping the commandments of the Lord. We glorify the goodness of God which hath been made manifest in thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Exapostilarion of the righteous one`},label:`glory`,saint:`Elizabeth`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Exapostilarion of the righteous one`,spec_mel:`The heaven with stars ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Having shone forth eternally, Light from Light, before the morning star, O Word, Thou didst come forth as Light, immutably, under time, from Thy Mother, illumining the ends of the world with radiant effulgence, as Thou art the Light of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the righteous one, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`The barren and childless Elizabeth didst Thou bless with fertility, O God, that Thou mayest reveal Thine almighty goodness. By Thy grace, have compassion upon us, who every day are withered by sins, that we may be aright fruitful tree, O Omnipotent One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,tone:1,repeat:2},{text:`The ever-memorable couple walked blamelessly in Thy commandments and through Thy grace were righteous in Thy sight, O compassionate One. All this was Thy mercy, O Master. Glory to Thy compassionate tender compassion!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`},{text:`God Who worketh within you that which He willed to accomplish, O right blessed couple, made you heirs to the Kingdom in His great mercy. Glory to Thee, O all-merciful Master!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`}],praises_glory:{text:`The greatest born of women is named by eternal Wisdom and hath come forth from thee, a barren woman, O God-loving Elizabeth. Let the faithful rejoice in the ever-memorable one, magnifying our Benefactor!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},praises_closer:{text:`He Who is hymned by the seraphim and borne up by the cherubim chose the womb of the pure divine maiden as a most beautiful throne. Wherefore, we send up to Thee this hymn of thanksgiving: Glory to Thee, O Thou Who alone lovest mankind! Glory to Thee, O Jesus all-sweet! Glory to Thee, O all our hope! Glory to Thee, salvation of the faithful! Glory to Thy compassionate dispensation!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Praises Both now`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., in Tone IV`,tone:4},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology, and the dismissal.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Great Doxology, and the dismissal.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakia`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of the canon of the holy prophet, and 4 from ODE VI of the canon of the righteous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`When thou didst offer the incense of the covenant, O high priest, then didst thou receive the prophetic proclamation of the Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`The priesthood anointed thee with oil to serve as a priest, like Aaron. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to behold the angel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zacharias begat John, the dawn which announced to the whole world Thee, the noetic Sun, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`When John was in thy womb, O holy Elizabeth, seeing His Savior he, the babe, did leap. Blessed is thy womb which made manifest the babe who recognized Jesus as his salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by the Holy Spirit against the will of others, O most blessed Elizabeth, thou didst name thy son John. Let everyone praise thee, the instrument of the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`O God, Thou didst show forth Elizabeth’s conceiving as an image of Thine own inconceivable birthgiving from the Virgin. Glory to Thy mighty wisdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`When he was born of Rachel, Benjamin caused his own mother’s death; but the Word Who was born of thee is the true life of all. Him do thou beseech, that we who place our trust in Him may have everlasting life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],kontakia:[{text:`Today Zacharias, the prophet and high priest of the Most High, * the father of the Forerunner, * setteth the table of his memorial, * feeding the faithful; * for he hath distributed the food of righteousness unto all. * Wherefore, he hath reposed * as a divine initiate ** of the mysteries of the grace of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Kontakion of the holy prophet at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Zacharias`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone III`,tone:3},{text:`Like the full moon, * thou didst receive the light of righteousness from the Messiah, * the noetic Sun, * O Elizabeth beloved of God, * and with Zacharias didst walk in all the commandments of the Lord. * Wherefore, blessing thee with worthy hymns, * we magnify the Lord, ** the most compassionate Light, Who illumineth all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Kontakion of the righteous one at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Elizabeth`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the righteous one, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],prokeimenon:{text:`The righteous man shall be glad in the Lord, * and shall hope in Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O God, unto my prayer, when I make supplication unto Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE HEBREWS,`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p19 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§314 (HEB.6: 13-20)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:6,verses:`13-20`,pericope_number:314},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`A light hath dawned for the righteous man, and gladness for the upright of heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p19 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. MATTHEW,`,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p19 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 96 (MT. 23: 29-39)`,citation:{book:`Matthew`,chapter:23,verses:`29-39`,pericope_number:96},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-05A.pdf`,locus:`p19 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"09-06":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.compline`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE MIRACLE PERFORMED BY THE ARCHANGEL MICHAEL AT COLOSSAE, WHICH IS ALSO KNOWN AS CHONAE. COMMEMORATION OF THE MARTYR EUDOXIUS AND THOSE WITH HIM.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 6th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`six_stichera`,fekula_section:`2C`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`09-06.pdf`,note:'OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). ODS 3rd ed. vol. III has no entry for 6 September (as V1 recorded). Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 6 stichera of the archangel (three printed, each "(Twice)"), a Glory, aposticha from the Oktoechos, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology rubric: Six-Stichera, Fekula 2C, agreeing with V1. Matins prints stichera ON THE PRAISES with a Glory AND THEN "On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos, and Glory": the same printed shape as 24 November (open question Q-0006), here in a service V1 and the waterfall both take as six-stichera. The martyr Eudoxius has a canon and stichera AT COMPLINE, tagged `saint: "Eudoxius"`; its troparia print "Glory ..." and "Both now ...," as inline labels, twice as "Glory ...O" with no comma or space. The Liturgy Gospel citation prints a capital letter O for the zero: "(1O:16-21)".',troparion:{text:`O supreme commander of the heavenly hosts, * we entreat thee unworthy though we be, * that by thy prayers, thou wilt encompass us * with the protection of the wings of thine immaterial glory * preserving us who fall down before thee and earnestly cry aloud: * deliver us from all misfortunes, ** for thou art the supreme commander of the hosts on high.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy archangel`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p14 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy archangel, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`O chief commander of God, minister of divine glory, * captain of the angels and instructor of all mankind: * beg thou great mercy and that which is profitable for us, * for thou art the supreme commander ** of the bodiless hosts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Kontakion of the holy archangel`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p10 after Ode VI`,tone:2},{locus:`p14 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy archangel, in Tone II`,tone:2},ikos:{text:`In Thy Scriptures, O immortal Lover of mankind, Thou didst say that a multitude of angels rejoiceth in heaven over one man that repenteth. Wherefore, O Sinless One, Who alone knowest the hearts of men, amid our transgressions we ever make bold to beseech Thee to have compassion and to send down compunction upon us, unworthy though we be, granting us forgiveness, O Master, in that Thou art compassionate; for the supreme commander of the bodiless hosts doth entreat Thee on behalf of us all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`“At Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera of the holy archangel, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O Michael, supreme commander, * shown forth as a most radiant intercessor before the three-Sunned Godhead, * thou dost cry out, rejoicing with the heavenly hosts: * Holy art Thou, O Father! * Holy art Thou, O co-beginningless Son! * Holy art Thou also, O Holy Spirit! * One glory, * one Kingdom and nature, ** one Godhead and power!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,repeat:2,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Thine aspect is fiery, * and thy beauty wondrous, * O Michael, first among angels, * for in thine immaterial nature * thou dost traverse the ends of the earth, * fulfilling the commandments of the Creator of all, * known in the power of thy might, * making thy church a wellspring of healings, ** revered in thy holy name.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`O Thou Who, as it is written, * doth make Thine angels spirits * and Thy ministers a flame of fire: * amid the ranks of Thine archangels, O Lord, * Thou hast shown forth as preeminent * Michael, the supreme commander, * who doth obey Thy commands, O Word, * and with fear doth utter ** the thrice-holy hymn unto Thy glory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Rejoice with us, all ye angelic legions, for the great supreme commander, your superior and our intercessor, appearing most wondrously this day in his honored temple, doth sanctify it. Wherefore, chanting as is meet, let us cry aloud to him: Cover us with the shelter of thy wings, O Michael, thou greatest of the archangels!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},composer:`the Byzantine`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI, the composition of the Byzantine`,tone:6},lic_closer:{text:`Rejoice with us, all ye choirs of virgins, for our intercessor, mediator, protection and great refuge doth today on her divine and honored feast comfort the sorrowful. Wherefore, hymning her at length as is meet, let us cry aloud: Protect us with thy divine intercession, O most pure Lady Theotokos!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:{absent:!0,reason:`governed_by_octoechos`,basis:`close_reading`,note:`The rubric appoints "the Stichera from the Oktoechos"; none are printed here.`,book:`octoechos`},aposticha_glory:{text:`O supreme commander, as general, champion and chief of the angels, from all want and grief, from afflictions and grievous sins do thou free those who hymn and beseech thee with faith, O glorious one, for thou art manifestly immaterial, beholding the Immaterial One, illumined with the unapproachable light of the Master’s glory. For in His love for mankind He took flesh from the Virgin for our sake, wishing to save the human race.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},composer:`John the Monk`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of John the Monk, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}},compline:{order:[`canon`,`sessional_ode6`,`stichera_rubric`,`stichera`,`stichera_closer`,`stichera_stavrotheotokion`],canon:{title:`Canon to the holy martyr Eudoxius, in Tone VIII:`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Having passed through the water as upon dry land, * and having escaped the malice of the Egyptians, * the Israelites cried aloud: * Unto our God and Redeemer let us sing.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ye who desire to proclaim the glories of the martyrs, come, let us all praise Eudoxius, great among martyrs, holding festival with cymbals as did David.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Throughout the whole world went the impious command not to worship the living God, but idols. But thou, O martyr, didst worship thy God, the God of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O martyr Eudoxius, thou glory of the pious, true to thy name, amidst the unjust judges that wounded thee didst thou confess Christ God Who is beginningless.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O Mother who did not know not a husband, the ranks of angels and mortals unceasingly praise thee, for thou didst bear their Creator in thine arms as a babe.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Christ fortify me on the rock of Thy commandments, * Thou who in the beginning didst establish the heavens with understanding * and didst establish the earth upon the waters, * for there is none holy save Thee, O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Like a lamb wast thou led to the slaughter, O martyr Eudoxius, neither protesting, nor crying out, O all-blessed one, emulating the life of Christ thy Teacher. Wherefore, thou hast received unending glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`To those who served idols thou didst cry out, O martyr: My God liveth forever, but your gods are the works of the hands of men; falling, they cannot rise up, for they are inanimate, graven images!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The arts of the enemy hast thou cast down, establishing thy mind upon the rock of the Church of Christ. Wherefore, thou didst cry aloud: This corruptible life do I leave for life everlasting!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...`,label_inline:!0},{text:`God the Word, co-enthroned and everlasting with the Father, wishing to restore the first of our race, took Adam’s hypostasis from thee, O pure one, finding thee to be the most holy of all women, O Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation; * I have considered Thy works, * and I have glorified Thy Divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst denounce the deception of those who sought to force thee to renounce everlasting life and to love a life of vanity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Wounded, thou didst rejoice in the Word Who was slain in the flesh for our sake, and thou didst cry aloud to thy tormentors: My sufferings are undeserved!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The gods whom ye serve have mouths, yet cannot speak! thou didst exclaim, O Eudoxius. Let those who fashion them be like unto them!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`As Thou art sinless, O Unknowable One, grant us purification, and bring calm to the world, O God, through the prayers of her who gaveth birth to Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Illumine us O Lord with Thy commandments, * and with Thine arm raised on high * grant us Thy peace, * O Lover of mankind!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou art my strength! Thou didst cry out, O Eudoxius. O Christ God Who suffered in the flesh, make me steadfast, for, lo! I suffer in torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art a treasury of entreaties, O Christ God! Disdain me not! didst thou cry amid the tortures, O Eudoxius, stout of heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Fearing neither the sword nor the fire, Eudoxius cried out to the tormentor: Behold, I have the mighty strength of the God I serve!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Heal thou the weakness of my passions, O pure one, making me worthy of thy visitation, and by thine entreaties grant me health.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Cleanse me, O Savior, * for many are mine iniquities; * lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee, * for unto Thee have I cried, * and Thou hast hearkened unto me, * O God of my salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Neither the sword, nor fire shall separate me from the love of Christ; and I hold your threats to be like the prating of children! didst thou cry out with faith to those who sought to compel thee to sacrifice.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`I fear that fire which doth torment and which cannot be quenched, and I desire that life which cannot be taken away! didst thou cry out to the tormentor, O Eudoxius. Behold, O thou who dost wound my body, I shall not serve thine idols!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The gods whom thou dost worship are gold and silver. They have mouths, but speak not; ears have they, yet hear not; legs they have, but cannot walk. But my God is the Creator of all! didst thou exclaim.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`By thy prayers may we be delivered from grievous transgressions, O pure Birthgiver of God, and may we acquire the radiance of the Son of God Who was ineffably incarnate from thee, O most holy one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The children of Judaea, * who of old came to dwell in Babylon, * trampled underfoot the flame of the furnace * through their faith in the Trinity, * as they sang: ‘O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst sail across an abyss of wounds and attain unto the harbor of life, O Eudoxius; and, receiving a crown of patience, with the angels thou dost unceasingly cry: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`To a place of rest hath Christ brought thee out who passed through fire and water, O blessed one; and rejoicing therein with the angels, O wise martyr, thou dost chant unceasingly a hymn to the Trinity: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people su-premely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst destroy the noetic serpent with the help of the King of heaven, O glorious one; and receiving a crown of victory and patience, unceasingly dost thou cry aloud with the immaterial ones: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The thrice-radiant Godhead which shineth forth in a single ray with one nature in three hypostases: the beginningless Father, the Word of one essence with the Father, and the consubstantial Spirit Who reigneth with them, ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In his wrath the Chaldean tyrant made the furnace blaze, * with heat fanned sevenfold for the servants of God; * but when he perceived that they had been saved by a greater power * he cried aloud to the Creator and Redeemer; * “Ye children bless, ye priests praise, * ye people, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages”.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Emulating the patience of the three youths, O most wise Eudoxius, thou didst not bend thy knee to the false image, but didst cry aloud with fervent faith: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Acquiring the invincible aid of grace, O martyr Eudoxius, thou didst firmly cast down the legions of the enemy, and having vanquished them thou didst cry aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Aflame with the love of divine desire, O martyr Eudoxius, thou didst openly abominate transitory attachments, and, receiving thy reward, thou didst cry out: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Our supremely good God, wishing to restore him that had fallen through deception, hath become incarnate and born of the Virgin, deifying mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Heaven was stricken with awe, * and the ends of the earth were filled with amazement, * for God hath appeared in the flesh, * and thy womb was rendered more spacious than the heavens. * Wherefore, the ranks of men and of angels * magnify thee as the Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The armies of the angels were struck with awe, and the assemblies of mortals were amazed that while possessing a corruptible and transitory nature thou didst reveal the demons to be wretched and weak; and with faith didst cry aloud: I shall serve the Trinity! Holy art Thou, O my Glory!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed art thou, O martyr Eudoxius, and glorified for all generations, for in no wise sparing thy flesh, thou didst endure torments for Christ’s sake and didst not bow down to graven images. Wherefore, the ranks of angels, clothed in the raiment of incorruption, have crowned thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy prayers unto God, O martyr Eudoxius, do thou rescue from every attack of the enemy those who with faith keep the memory of thy sufferings, that he may not boast over us; for, as a martyr, thou art able to do this, having received a reward for thy sufferings from the Most High.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O Virgin Mother of God, thou hast been revealed to be her who hath given birth in the flesh unto God the Word, to Whom the Father, in that He is good, gave utterance from His own heart before all the ages, and Who is now known to be higher than all bodies, even though He hath clothed Himself in a body.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}]}}},sessional_ode6:[{text:`Having amassed heavenly riches, thou didst scatter them, offering them to the poor; and thy bread didst thou give unto the hungry. Wherefore, having acquired incorruptible life, thou didst shine forth in thy confession of Christ. Therefore, taking courage and suffering under the law, thou hast received from God a crown for thy labors, O passion-bearer Eudoxius. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love honor thy sacred memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p4-p5 Compline sessional after Ode VI`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eudoxius`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8}],stichera_rubric:{text:`Stichera of the holy martyr, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Stichera of the holy martyr`}},stichera:[{text:`For thy virtues thou didst receive from the Savior grace befitting thy name, O martyr Eudoxius, and right boldly didst exchange thy life for the glory of martyrdom, and joining chorus with the angels in the heavens thou hast now been glorified as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Stichera 1`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eudoxius`,tone:1,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`For the severing of thy neck for the sake of thy faith thou didst crown thy head with a heavenly crown, O most blessed Eudoxius. Wherefore, cease not in thy prayers to Christ, that He remember us who keep thy memory, O glorious martyr.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Stichera 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eudoxius`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Spurning wealth and this transitory life, O Eudoxius, like Moses thou didst reckon the bearing of Christ’s burden a divine boast greater than the glory of the world, O glorious one, approaching tortures and trials even to the shedding of thy blood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Stichera 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eudoxius`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],stichera_closer:{text:`Tempest-tossed on the abyss of transgressions, * fleeing to the calm haven * of thy most pure supplication, * I cry out to thee, O Theotokos: ** Save me, O most immaculate one, extending thy mighty right hand unto thy servant!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Stichera Glory/Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion in Tone I`,tone:1},stichera_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Standing at the foot of the Cross * of thy Son and God, * and looking upon His long-suffering, * O pure Mother, * weeping, thou didst say: * “Woe is me, O my sweetest Child! * How is it that Thou sufferest these things unjustly, * O Word of God, ** that Thou mayest save mankind?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Stichera Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`praises_rubric`,`praises`,`praises_glory`,`praises_closer_rubric`,`praises_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without the martyria, and this canon of the holy archangel, with 6 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn the first of the bodiless intelligences,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without the martyria, and this canon of the holy archangel, with 6 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn the first of the bodiless intelligences,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone IV:`,composer:`Joseph`,acrostic:`I hymn the first of the bodiless intelligences`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`I shall open my mouth, * and be filled with the Spirit, * and utter discourse to the Queen and Mother; * and be seen radiantly keeping festival, * joyfully praising her wonders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O supreme commander of the armies of heaven, ever illumined with divine splendors, enlighten my mind, that I may hymn thee, O thou who art the confirmation of those who have recourse unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The beginningless Mind showed thee, O most glorious supreme commander, to be the general of the supra-ordinary ranks, a light unto those who are in darkness and a divine adornment of His Church.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Surpassing the heavenly intelligences in spirit, O most eminent Michael, thou wast given to them below as a wall of defense, confirmation, a weapon which slayeth and destroyeth the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-immaculate Virgin, thou splendor of the angels and aid of mortals, help me who sail the sea and ever venture into the tempest of sin and danger.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Not in wisdom, nor in power do we glory, * but we glory in Thee O Christ, * the Hypostatic Wisdom of the Father, * for there is none more holy than Thee, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With divine might dost thou encircle all the earth, O all-praised chief among the angels, rescuing us who call upon thy divine name, from the cruel enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O supreme commander of God, of aspect most divine, thou hast been a divine herald, an undaunted intercessor for the faithful, a guide to those who are astray and an instructor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast a most pure mirror of the splendor of God, radiantly reflecting the manifestation of the honored Spirit, O right wondrous Michael, first among the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`He that by His own will wrought the immaterial intelligences made His abode within thy divine womb as was His desire, O all-immaculate one. The Un-seeable is seen in the flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`He who sitteth in glory upon the throne of the Godhead, * Jesus the true God, * is come in a swift cloud * and with His sinless hands he hath saved those who cry: * Glory to Thy power, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Being Thyself the supreme Intelligence, by Thy will Thou didst create the divine intelligences and in their midst didst set Michael as a leader illumined with all-blessed fellowship and radiant with the noetic ordinances of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Michael most glorious, thou dost give utterance unto a holy hymn with the thrones, principalities, powers, authorities and sacred dominions, saving us who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`We magnify the Creator and Lord of all Who, in His tender compassion hath given us the luminous supreme commander Michael as a safeguard most great, an unassailable rampart and tower.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Of old the teacher of sacred truths noetically described the mystery of thy birthgiving, O Virgin, beholding thee most clearly in the Spirit as a mountain overshadowed, from whence our holy God hath come forth incarnate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`The wicked will not behold Thy glory, O Christ, * but we who rise early to hymn Thee shall behold Thee, * the Only-Begotten effulgence of Thy Father’s divinity, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O incorporeal Michael, supreme commander of the angels, thou didst appear lead-ing Israel of old at the command of Him Who hath come forth out of Jacob and hath appeared unto all in the coarseness of a body.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ever deified by immaterial splendors by partaking of the divine, and wondrously amazed, thou dost bestow enlightening radiance upon us, O thou who art first among the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy divine temple is adorned with grace, for, entering therein, thou didst show it forth to be an abyss of healings and a destroyer of passions, O Michael, first among the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`God hath shown thee to be more exalted than the noetic angels, having made His abode within thy womb, O pure and all-immaculate one. Him do thou ever beseech, that He take pity on those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Prefiguring Thy three-day burial * prophet Jonah praying in the belly of the sea-monster cried aloud: * Deliver me from corruption * O Jesus Thou King of hosts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The multitude of the faithful rejoiceth, praising thee, O Michael, and it doth glorify the all-holy Word Who in His goodness hath united mortals and angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst save the armies of Israel, revealing thyself and transmitting the commands of God, O supreme commander; casting down enemies and utterly destroying them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Seized with fear and reverence, Joshua, son of Nun, bowed down when he beheld, thee, O chief of the angels, asking thine honored and holy name.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed are the people who ever bless thee, O blessed one, who hast given birth unto the blessed God, Who, in His tender compassion, hath deified mortal mankind by an ineffable union.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst save the children of Abraham in the fire * and slay the Chaldeans, * who unjustly entrapped the righteous ones. * O supremely hymned Lord, God of our fathers, * blessed art Thou.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Beholding, Daniel saw thee, O blessed Gabriel of lightning-bright visage, standing together with Michael, the supreme commander, who commanded thee to cause him to understand the vision which he had seen by the banks of the Ulai.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With faith let us shout the praises of the radiant Michael and Gabriel, chiefs among the angels that behold God, our good comforters, intercessors and protectors.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Being comely, most splendid and of godly aspect, in a manner surpassing understanding art thou the chief of the immaterial spirits, O most radiant Michael; with them, therefore, pray thou on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Beholding the truly ever-existent Word of the great Mind making His abode within thee in a strange and ineffable manner, O Virgin, the archangel Gabriel cried aloud: Rejoice, O blessed throne of the Most High!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O almighty Redeemer of all, * having descended and bedewed the children * in the midst of the flame, * Thou didst teach them to sing: * All ye works bless and hymn the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Michael, thou hast been shown to be a commander of the noetic and incorporeal hosts, a saving intercessor for all mankind, a divine servant of God, chanting unceasingly: All ye works, bless and hymn the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O archangels Gabriel and Michael, two beacons most radiant, enlightening creation with the splendor of the thrice-radiant Godhead: dispel ye the gloom of the wicked.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O archangels, as good helmsmen to the harbor of the divine will bring ye safely the ship of my soul which hath encountered a tempest of sins and is in distress.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Standing before thee, the archangel, as divine adorner of the bride, greeted thee: Rejoice, unwedded Bride of God, thou glory of the angels, salvation and defense of mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Eve dwelt under the curse of sin * because of the infirmity of disobedience; * but thou, O Virgin Theotokos, * hast through the Offspring of thy pregnancy * blossomed forth blessing upon the world. * Wherefore, we all magnify thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Behold, O archangel, the resplendent magnificence of thy divine temple which putteth forth lightning flashes of miracles through thy radiant presence, ever dispelling the darkness of infirmities with divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a comely and beauteous pair ye minister unto those who are on earth at the behest of the Master, O archangels, rescuing them from evil circumstances and sending down divine illumination upon all through the Spirit of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today the incorporeal and divine intelligences rejoice with us, beholding their great and splendid supreme commander hymned by all; and with us they lovingly keep festival, magnifying the Bestower of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O archangels, divine and radiant pair, Michael most honorable and Gabriel supremely glorious; interceding before the honored Trinity, deliver us who praise you from torment and the cause of transgression.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Joyously we offer thee the cry of the divine Gabriel, exclaiming: Rejoice, most pure paradise which hath within thee the Tree of life, thou most glorious palace of the Word! Rejoice, O all-immaculate Virgin!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having become, as is meet, the leader of the ranks of heaven and minister of the glory of God, by the command of thy Creator, thou art a saving mediator, watching over mortals with thine immaterial glory. Wherefore, we all praise thee as is due, chanting the hymns of thy divine feast today, O supreme commander Michael. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins to those who lovingly hymn thy divine wonders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p8-p9 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`The choir of angels, having the divine Michael as its supreme commander, doth offer with him unceasing hymnody unto the Holy Trinity, for the Creator of all by His word brought the fiery ranks into being, out of non-existence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode III sessional, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., another Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`The choir of angels ...`,tone:1},{text:`O most holy Virgin, hope of Christians, with the hosts on high do thou unceasingly beseech God to Whom, in a manner surpassing understanding and all telling, thou hast given birth, that He grant forgiveness of all our sins and correction of life unto those who with faith and love ever glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1},{text:`Upon seeing the Lamb and Shepherd hanging dead upon the Tree, * the unblemished ewe-lamb, cried aloud, weeping * and exclaiming maternally: * “How is it that Thou dost willingly endure abasement and sufferings * which surpass all telling, ** O my Son, and supremely good God?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`As of old thou didst subdue the raging flow and thundering of the river, O glorious supreme commander, so now destroy the pride of the heathen and the raging of the demons, that we may fittingly honor thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy archangel`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`The ranks of the bodiless hosts honor thy birthgiving, for thou alone hast filled mortals with joy. Wherefore, we, the faithful, glorify thee the all-immaculate one, singing the praises of thy glory in hymns, for thou hast shone forth light upon those who are in darkness, like the dawn which shineth forth in the morning.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, these Stichera, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Keeping festival in the world like angels, * let us give voice unto a hymn to God * Who sitteth upon the throne of glory: * Holy art Thou, O heavenly Father! * Holy art Thou, O equally everlasting Son! ** Holy art Thou also, O all-holy Spirit!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`O Michael, supreme commander, * who dost thyself behold ineffable things, * who in boldness art pre-eminent among the many inhabitants of heaven, * standing before the dread throne in glory: * by thy prayers save us who find ourselves amid want, ** misfortune and temptations, we beseech thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Truly thou art first among the incorporeal angels, * a minister of the divine effulgence of God, * an initiate of the mysteries of God * who dost thyself behold Him. * O Michael, supreme commander, save us who each year piously honor thee ** and hymn the Trinity with faith!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`Michael, the commander of the host on high, pre-eminent among the divine ranks, hath summoned us today to his festival. He is ever with us, preserving all from every evil circumstance wrought by the devil. Come ye, therefore, O ye who love the feasts of the Church and who love Christ, and, taking up the flowers of the virtues, with pure thoughts and an upright conscience let us honor the assembly of the archangels, for, ever standing before God and chanting the thrice-holy hymn, they pray that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone I`,tone:1},praises_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises Both now rubric`}},praises_stavrotheotokion:{text:`‘A sword hath pierced me, O my Son,’ * said the Virgin upon seeing Christ hung upon the Tree, * ‘my heart hath been rent O Lord, * as Simeon once foretold to me. * But arise, I pray Thee, O immortal One, ** and glorify Thy Mother and handmaiden.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:1,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},aposticha_glory:{text:`Where thy grace doth shine forth, O archangel, thence is the power of the devil driven away, for the fallen morning star cannot endure the sight of thy light. Wherefore, we entreat thee: by thy mediation quench thou the fiery darts which he launcheth against us, and deliver us from his snares, O right lauded Michael, supreme commander!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Matins Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos, and Glory ..., in Tone V`,tone:5},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Matins Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon seeing her Lamb hastening to the slaughter * the Ewe-lamb eagerly followed Him crying aloud: * ‘Whence goest Thou, O my sweetest Child? * O most beloved Jesus, * sinless Lord, rich in mercy, * O longsuffering Christ, * why dost Thou so swiftly and so fearlessly proceed? * Speak to me Thy handmaiden, * O my well-beloved Son: * pass not by me, Thy Mother, without a word, * O all-compassionate God, ** who grantest the world great mercy.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Matins Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:5,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: four each from Odes III and VI of the canon of the holy archangel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`With divine might dost thou encircle all the earth, O all-praised chief among the angels, rescuing us that call upon thy divine name from the cruel enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O supreme commander of God, of aspect most divine, thou hast been a divine herald, an undaunted intercessor for the faithful, a guide to those who are astray and an instructor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast a most pure mirror of the splendor of God, radiantly reflecting the manifestation of the honored Spirit, O right wondrous Michael, first among the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The multitude of the faithful rejoiceth, praising thee, O Michael, and it doth glorify the most holy Word Who in His goodness hath united men and angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst save the armies of Israel, revealing thyself and transmitting the commands of God, O supreme commander; and thou didst cast down the enemy and didst utterly destroy them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Seized with fear and reverence, Joshua, son of Nun, bowed down when he beheld, thee, O chief of the angels, asking thine honored and holy name.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed are the people that ever bless thee, O blessed one, who hast given birth unto the blessed God, Who, in His tender compassion, hath deified mortal man by an ineffable union.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`He maketh His angels spirits, * and His ministers a flame of fire.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Bless the Lord, O my soul; O Lord my God, Thou hast been magnified exceedingly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`THE EPISTLE OF PAUL THE APOSTLE TO THE HEBREWS`,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(2:2-10)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:2,verses:`2-10`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Praise Him, all ye His angels; praise Him, all ye His hosts.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone V`,label_inline:!0,tone:5},alleluia_verse:{text:`For He spake, and they came to be; He commanded, and they were created.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`READING FROM THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(1O:16-21)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:10,verses:`16-21`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`He maketh His angels spirits, and His ministers a flame of fire.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"09-07":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`forefeast`,feast_ref:`nativity_theotokos`,title:{text:`FOREFEAST OF THE NATIVITY OF THE MOST HOLY THEOTOKOS COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYR SOZON`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 7th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`six_stichera`,fekula_section:`2G1`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`09-07.pdf`,note:'OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). ODS 3rd ed. vol. III has no entry for 7 September (as V1 recorded). ONE printed service for the Forefeast of the Nativity of the Theotokos and the Martyr Sozon: one entry, items tagged `saint` ("forefeast" / "Sozon"). 3 stichera of the forefeast and 3 of the martyr; no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology (Matins ends with Aposticha). RANK FOLLOWS V1 (six_stichera, Fekula 2G1) so the comparison starts level; by the 1.1 waterfall as applied to 11-20 and 11-22 the same shape was stored `simple` under 2G1. 2G1 covers both, so the section agrees; the rank word is a difference between V1 and the November entries TO BE SETTLED at the wire-in. Two canons (forefeast, by Joseph; martyr, by Theophanes), stored whole. The forefeast canon prints no theotokion label in its odes. Two troparia and two kontakia at every print site in positional lists. The Liturgy propers printed are the martyr\'s only.',vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`lic_closer_alternate_rubric`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparia`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera: 3 of the forefeast, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Noetic beams of universal joy * have shone forth upon the world, * heralding Christ God, the Sun of righteousness unto all, * through thy nativity O most pure one. * For thou hast been revealed to be ** the mediatress of true gladness and grace.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`,saint:`forefeast`,tone:1},{text:`This, the glory of thy forefeast, O most pure one, * doth proclaim unto all the people * thy benefactions which transcend description; * for thou hast become for us the mediatress of gladness * and the cause of joy to come, ** O Ever-virgin Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`,saint:`forefeast`},{text:`The maiden who held God within her womb, * the pure Theotokos, * the glory of the prophets, the daughter of David * is born today of Joachim and the chaste Anna; * and the curse of Adam which lay upon us ** is annulled by her nativity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`,saint:`forefeast`},{text:`When He Who of His own will * took our weakness upon Himself, * He strengthened thine infirmity with power, O blessed one, * for His sake thou didst run the race of martyrdom, rejoicing, * and with thy most beautiful feet * didst crush the impotent enemy. * Wherefore, Jesus, the Lover of mankind, * the Savior of our souls, ** hath woven wreaths of victory for thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`And 3 Stichera of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`,tone:4},{text:`When thou wast wounded, O glorious one, * thou didst wound thine enemies * and cast them down to the ground, * armed with the Cross * and manifestly arrayed in invincible armor, * made steadfast by the love * of Him Who hath translated thee to the noetic kingdoms * as an unvanquished martyr, ** and a heavenly man.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`Manifestly emulating * the Savior and Lord * Who for thee underwent voluntary sufferings, * O spiritual athlete Sozon, * thou didst of thine own will give thyself over * to wounds and stripes and unbearable torments. * Wherefore, He hath honored thee with heavenly gifts * and showed thee forth as a well-spring of healings ** for those who love thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`}],lic_closer:{text:`O Virgin most holy and pure, we, the multitude of angels in heaven and the race of mankind on earth, bless thy most honored nativity, in that thou didst become the Mother of Christ God, the Creator of all. Cease thou never to entreat Him, we pray, on behalf of us who, after God, have placed our trust in thee, O all-praised Theotokos who knewest not wedlock.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now, of the forefeast`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., of the forefeast, in Tone IV`,tone:4},lic_closer_alternate_rubric:{text:`But if it be Friday evening: Glory ..., the above Doxasticon of the Forefeast; Both now ..., the Dogmaticon of the current tone.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 If it be Friday evening`}},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the forefeast, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`O most glorious wonder! * The rod which is to bear the Flower * springeth forth today from the righteous Joachim and Anna, * from a barren mother * and a fruitless womb, O Mother of God * Who knewest not wedlock. * Wherefore, the council of the prophets * and the whole festive assembly of the patriarchs ** rejoice now in her nativity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Today David doth rejoice, * Jesse now danceth, * Levi is magnified, * and the righteous Joachim rejoiceth in spirit: * for the childlessness of Anna is loosed * by thy nativity, O most pure Mary, * divinely joyous one. * And all of us, the assembly of angels and men, ** call thy divine womb blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`The rich among the people * shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Rejoice, O assembly of men! Rejoice, O temple of the Lord! * Rejoice, holy mountain! Rejoice, divine table! * Rejoice, O lamp of the Light! * Rejoice, O honored glory of the Orthodox! * Rejoice, O Mary, Mother of Christ God! * Rejoice, O all-immaculate one! * Rejoice, offering of the Bread divine! * Rejoice, O tabernacle! Rejoice, O bush unburnt! ** Rejoice thou hope of all!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Universal joy hath shone forth upon us from the righteous Joachim and Anna, O all-praised Virgin who, in thine exceeding purity, didst become the animate temple of God, and who alone art truly known to be the Theotokos. Through her prayers, O Christ God, grant peace unto the world and great mercy unto our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,composer:`Germanus`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of Germanus, in Tone IV`,tone:4},troparia:[{text:`In his sufferings, Thy martyr Sozon O Lord, * received an imperishable crown from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * he set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By his supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Mary, the divine maiden, is born unto us today * from the root of Jesse and the loins of David; * and all things rejoice and are made new through joy. * Rejoice together, O heaven and earth! * Praise her, ye lands of the gentiles! * Joachim maketh glad, and Anna holdeth festival, crying aloud: ** A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the Nourisher of our Life!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the forefeast`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`of_the_feast`],saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Troparion of the forefeast, in Tone IV`,tone:4}]},matins:{order:[`troparia`,`troparia_closing_rubric`,`sessional_1`,`sessional_2`,`canons`,`kontakia_ode3`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakia_ode6`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`],troparia:[{text:`Mary, the divine maiden, is born unto us today * from the root of Jesse and the loins of David; * and all things rejoice and are made new through joy. * Rejoice together, O heaven and earth! * Praise her, ye lands of the gentiles! * Joachim maketh glad, and Anna holdeth festival, crying aloud: ** A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the Nourisher of our Life!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Troparion of the forefeast at God is the Lord`},label:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the forefeast`},{text:`In his sufferings, Thy martyr Sozon O Lord, * received an imperishable crown from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * he set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By his supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Troparion of the holy martyr at God is the Lord`},label:`glory`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., that of the holy martyr in Tone IV`,tone:4}],troparia_closing_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., that of the forefeast (Once).`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Both now, that of the forefeast (Once)`}},sessional_1:[{text:`Having been born most gloriously from the womb of a barren woman, thou didst give birth from thy virginal womb in a manner transcending nature; for, revealed as a beautiful stem, thou didst give rise to the Life of the world. Wherefore, the hosts of heaven cry out to thee, O Theotokos: Glory to thine advent, O pure one! Glory to thy nativity! Glory to thy virginity, O Mother who hast not known wedlock!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 1`},spec_mel:`When the stone had been sealed ...`,label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`After the first chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 1 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],sessional_2:[{text:`All those of heaven now rejoice, and the human race doth now keep festival with them. The prophets mystically are glad; for she whom they foresaw in generations of old in the images of the bush, the jar and the staff, the cloud, the portal, the throne and the great mountain - is born today.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`After the second chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone V`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word ...`,tone:5},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 2 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],canons:[{title:`Canon of the forefeast, with 8 Troparia, including its Irmos, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn the nativity of the divine Virgin”, composition of Joseph, in Tone IV:`,composer:`Joseph`,tone:4,acrostic:`I hymn the nativity of the divine Virgin`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`I shall open my mouth, * and be filled with the Spirit, * and utter discourse to the Queen and Mother; * and be seen radiantly keeping festival, * joyfully praising her wonders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Rejoicing today, let us with gladness hymn the divine nativity of the Mother of God; for she hath given birth to the Joy of the universe which destroyeth the grief of our first mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`From a barren woman doth the most pure and all-immaculate Lady issue forth barren of sin, whom the law prefigured and the proclamations of the divine heralds of God announced.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The temple and palace of the King didst thou become, wherein, fashioning a habitation for Himself, the Transcendent One hath made for the faithful a dwelling-place of the Holy Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The most comely wedding chamber, the most exalted throne of God, whereon the Transcendent One hath seated Himself in the flesh, hath issued forth from a barren woman; raising up those who sit in the darkness of perdition, unto the knowledge of the Light, by His exceeding goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Likened to a barren woman * the Church from among the nations hath given birth, * and the assembly abundant in children, hath grown weak. * Let us cry out to our wondrous God: * Holy art Thou, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`A fertile land is born from a barren land, bearing as fruit the Husbandman of all good things, the life-bearing Grain Who nourisheth all by His divine providence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today hath the rod of virginity sprouted forth, from whence our God, the Gardener, hath blossomed forth as a flower, cutting down the branches of wickedness by His extreme beauty.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Lo! the mountain unquarried, which arose from a barren rock, produceth the noetically quarried Stone, Who crusheth the delusion of all graven idols.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`He who sitteth in glory upon the throne of the Godhead, * Jesus the true God, * is come in a swift cloud * and with His sinless hands he hath saved those who cry: * Glory to Thy power, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The maiden who is more exalted than the angels is born on earth, in holiness and purity beyond compare; and she giveth birth unto Christ, the purification, sanctification and perfect deliverance of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed was the fruit of Anna; for she bore in her womb her who would contain the blessed and infinite Word Who bestoweth regeneration upon all the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Now doth the gloom of evil begin to break, for the all-immaculate one, the animate cloud of the Sun, hath shone forth from a barren womb, and this, her radiant nativity, we celebrate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a fruitful olive-tree sprung forth from the root of Jesse, O Virgin, hath Anna first given birth unto thee who will cause the merciful Word to spring forth. His mercy and truth abide forever.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`All creation stands in awe of thy divine glory; * for thou, O Virgin who hast not known wedlock, * didst contain within thy womb the God of all, * and gave birth to the timeless Son, * bestowing peace, upon all who hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Now is the book which shall remain sealed born, that which is impossible for mortals to fathom, because it is contrary to natural law, but which is to be kept as the dwelling-place of the Word, that book which by the Spirit shall be revealed to the divinely eloquent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The vine of salvation is born today, which blossomed forth the divine Cluster of incorruption, pouring forth sweetness; and everyone, drinking mystically thereof, shall bring forth divine and salvific gladness as fruit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Leap up, O mortals, join ye chorus with the angels! For the Virgin is born today from the barren woman, sadness hath come to an end and been transformed into joy for those who celebrate her divine nativity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Most manifestly did the prophet describe thee as a new and divine scroll, upon which the Word is to be written by the finger of the Father, O Virgin, in His goodness inscribing in the Book of Life all who submit to His authority.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Celebrating the divine and solemn feast * of the Mother of God * O ye divinely wise, * let us come, clapping our hands, * and glorify God who was born of her.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Today the bridge which leadeth mankind to the Light is born, the ladder of heaven, the most manifest mountain of God, the Virgin Theotokos, whom we call blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Anna, the shell of all purple, hath given rise to the purple which will later dye the fleece of the King’s incarnation. Her do we all hymn as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A well-spring hath now issued forth from the littlest drop: the all-immaculate one who, having given birth to the Abyss of salvation, hath caused the boundless streams of polytheism to cease.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst spring forth from a barren root, O ever-blessed Virgin Birthgiver of God, and by thy divine budding forth hast cut off at the root the thorns of wickedness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Refusing to worship created things * in place of the Creator, * the divinely wise youths bravely trampled down the threatening fire * and rejoicing they sang aloud: * O supremely hymned Lord and God of our Fathers, Blessed art Thou.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Blessed are Joachim and Anna, who manifestly gave birth to the blessed and pure Mother of God who hath given birth to the blessed Word Who rendereth all the faithful blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a precious gift thy parents acquired thee who conceived God, Who hath enriched with better gifts those who cry aloud: O Lord and God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`More blessed than wine are thy breasts, O divinely called Anna; for with sacred breasts thou didst nurture with milk her who gaveth suck to the supremely good Word, the Bestower of milk, the Nourisher of all things that have breath.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely inspired David, leap up, strike thy psaltery and dance! For, lo! the ark which of old thou didst proclaim hath come forth from a barren womb, reserved for the King and God of creation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Offspring of the Theotokos * saved the holy children in the furnace. * He who was then prefigured hath now been born on earth, * and He gathereth all creation to hymn thee: * all ye works praise ye the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Let us move our tongues in hymnody, honoring the divine nativity of her who, through the Spirit, rendered incarnate the supremely divine Word; and let us cry aloud: Hymn the Lord, ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Leap up, ye prophets of God, honoring the nativity of the Virgin; for she hath fulfilled the prophecy of all of you, giving birth to Christ, the God of all, Who was foretold by you. Him do ye supremely exalt throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ye mountains, resound with gladness! O apostles and martyrs, join chorus! Ye venerable and righteous, rejoice today in the nativity of the Mother of the Lord, cry out: Hymn the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The all-pure Mother of the Word hath blossomed forth as a fragrant apple; she hath appeared as a divine rose, perfuming the ends of the world today and banishing the cause of our sin. Her do we supremely exalt throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Human nature, bereft of the precious gifts of the divine Spirit, was made glad on this day, seeing the divine maiden born of a barren woman; and it crieth aloud: Hymn the Lord, ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 5`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Let every mortal born on earth, * radiant with light, in spirit leap for joy; * and let the host of the angelic powers * celebrate and honor the holy feast of the Mother of God, * and let them cry aloud: * Rejoice! O all-blessed Theotokos, * thou pure Ever-virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Lo! the holy place of God hath been shown forth! The exceedingly glorious city of the King hath been erected! The luminous garden of paradise hath splendidly blossomed forth her who is the mediatress of paradise, the point of reconciliation between God and man.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today hath the lamp of the Light appeared, in which the pre-eternal Light of golden luster, having taken up His abode, illumining those who languish in the night of evils, destroying the gloom of ungodliness, and truly leading all to share in the day, because of their faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today the earth joineth in chorus, for it hath seen the new and most comely heaven of God born. And dwelling therein in the flesh, He hath raised up mankind higher than the heavens and deifieth all in His goodness. Chanting, we magnify Him with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Joachim and Anna, the most comely pair, have given rise to the unblemished heifer. And the fatted Calf Who came forth from her hath been slain for the world, taking upon Himself the transgressions of mankind and destroying the sacrifices offered to the demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Birthgiver of God, who hast given birth to the Light, illumine us who in the Spirit celebrate thy radiant nativity, and show us to be participants in the light which is to come; and by thy maternal supplications, O most pure one, grant us peace and deliverance from evils.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 5`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon of the holy martyr, with 4 Troparia, by Theophanes, in Tone IV:`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Through the deep of the Red Sea, * marched dry shod Israel of old, * and by Moses’ outstretched hands, * raised in the form of a cross, * the power of Amalek was routed in the wilderness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O most glorious one, entreat now the Lord and Benefactor, that those who honor thy memory today be saved from all manner of dangers, tribulations and sorrows; and do thou help them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ hath truly revealed thee to be a most radiant star in the firmament of the Church, O all-famed martyr, illumining the whole world with the splendors of thy sufferings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having roiled the sea of impiety as a steed of the Lord, O martyr, in the abyss of thy precious and holy blood thou didst drown all the power of the adversary, as if another Pharaoh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`By the will of the Father, through the divine Spirit, didst thou conceive the Son of God without seed and give birth in the flesh unto Him Who existeth from the Father without mother and Who for our sake, was born of thee without a father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Thy Church, O Christ, rejoiceth in Thee crying aloud: * Thou, O Lord, art my strength, * my refuge and foundation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The streams of thy blood, flowing forth like a river for Christ’s sake, have quenched the fire of the impious, O ever-hymned martyr and spiritual athlete.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst patiently endure the infliction of wounds, like an impregnable tower, O glorious one, bringing down the fortress of deception.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like David thou didst bring low the noetic Goliath, the tyrant and his army, with the stone of faith, O all-glorious one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Mother of God, thou alone hast in a manner transcending nature shown thyself to be the mediatress of good things. Wherefore, we cry out to thee: Rejoice!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Beholding Thee, the Sun of righteousness, * lifted up upon the Cross, * the Church now standeth arrayed and doth worthily cry aloud: * Glory be to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Set afire by the love of God, O all-blessed one, with thy words thou didst utterly consume all the tinder-like fuel of the ungodly; and, rejoicing, thou didst cry aloud: Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a sanctified temple of the Lord, thou didst run into the temple of the ungodly and manfully break the objects of their worship, O all-praised spiritual athlete and martyr.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy sacred temple hath been shown to be the healing of all manner of illnesses for those who have recourse to it in faith and who honor thy valiant deeds therein, O all-famed spiritual athlete Sozon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast given birth unto the Lord without knowing wedlock, O Virgin, and after thy birthgiving wast shown to remain a Virgin. Wherefore, with unwavering faith and never silent voices we cry out to thee, O Lady: Rejoice!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, who camest into the world, * art my light, * a holy Light turning from the darkness of ignorance * those who sing Thy praises in faith.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou, O martyr, illumined by the light of the Trinity, didst destroy the gloom of the ungodliness of polytheism, as an ever-radiant beacon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shown to be a rose of comely blossom by the flow of thy blood, O blessed one, thou hast perfumed the world with the sweet fragrance of thy miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a noetic cluster of the vineyard of Christ, thou hast poured forth the right-compunctionate wine of martyrdom upon those who glorify thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We hold thee as an invincible weapon against the enemy, and we have thee as the foundation and hope of our salvation, O Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The Church crieth out unto Thee O Lord, * ‘I will sacrifice unto Thee with a voice of praise’ * having been cleansed of the blood of the demons’ * by the blood that for mercy’s sake flowed from Thy side.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Desiring to be slain as an unblemished sacrifice, for the sake of God’s love, thou didst offer thyself up on His altar. Wherefore, we piously honor thee, O all-famed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having sailed over the deep of deception without foundering, thou didst attain unto the calm haven of the kingdom on high, O blessed martyr, enjoying everlasting quietude.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The tormenter pitilessly raked thy sides with claws of iron; but thou didst gloriously commit thy spirit into the hands of God, O ever memorable and all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O wonder more recent than all wonders! The Virgin conceived in her womb, without knowing a man, Him Who sustaineth all things, yet did not confine Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`In the Persian furnace the youths and descendants of Abraham, * burning with a love of piety * rather than by a flame of fire, * cried aloud saying: * Blessed art Thou in the temple of Thy glory, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Cast into the furnace of painful torments, O martyr, thou didst receive from God the dew of endurance, and didst cry out in thanksgiving: Blessed art Thou in the temple of Thy glory, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Possessed of a soul more luminous than any gold, thou didst in no wise desire to sacrifice to the soulless gods of beaten gold, but rather offered thyself to the Lord as a sacrifice of sweet savor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The great Shepherd appointed thee, His unblemished lamb, as shepherd for the sheep of his true flock, O martyr, showing thee un-devoured by the noetic wolves, O all-praised one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O hallowed and divine habitation of the Most High For through thee, O Theotokos, hath joy been given to those who cry aloud: Blessed art thou among women, O all-immaculate Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Having spread his hands, Daniel closed the lions’ jaws * in their den; * while the zealously pious youths, * girded with virtue, * quenched the power of the fire and cried aloud: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Removing the arm of the golden idol, O wise one, thou didst distribute it among the poor, securing for thyself the truly incalculable riches of martyrdom, O ever-memorable one who cried aloud: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When the incorporeal foe wrestled with thee, thou didst cast him down with the assistance of Christ. Wherefore, He Himself hath bestowed honors upon thee: the ability to work miracles. To Him didst thou cry out, rejoicing: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Opening thy mouth, thou didst fill it with the Spirit, O all-praised Sozon, and the mouths of those who blaspheme the Creator didst thou fill with all manner of shame; and, rejoicing, thou didst cry out to Christ: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Among all generations, O pure Virgin, thou alone hast been revealed to be the Mother of God. Thou wast the receptacle of God, O all-immaculate one, who wast not consumed by the fire of the unapproachable Light. Wherefore, we all call thee blessed, O Mary, Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`A cornerstone not cut by hand O Virgin, * was cut from thee the unhewn mountain: * even Christ, Who hath joined together the disparate natures; * therefore rejoicing we magnify thee, * O Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Cast down to the ground, thou wast shown to be a chosen stone of Christ the Chief Cornerstone, O martyr, destroying the fortress of deception, and making firm the hearts of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Church of Christ, having now acquired thee as a stream of life, is ever adorned with the majesty of thy sufferings and miracles, O martyr, having quenched its thirst with thy blood as with water.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst find the kingdom of heaven to be the reward of thy struggles and labors, O divinely wise Sozon. Joining chorus therein, O all-glorious one, be thou mindful of those who with faith keep thy sacred memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Loose thou now the chains of mine offenses, O Virgin Theotokos who hast given birth to the Source of tender compassion; and fill me with joy, O thou who alone art blessed of God, that I may magnify thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`Assembling today, with a loud voice let us praise Sozon, * the true and divinely wise martyr, * the skilled spiritual athlete of piety, * the initiate of the mysteries of grace, * the most generous bestower of healings: * for he entreateth Christ God ** on behalf of us all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy martyr (after Ode III)`},spec_mel:`The steadfast ...`,label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyr, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`Come ye, and with hymns let us all now earnestly praise Sozon offering worthy hymns unto the great spiritual athlete who hath shone forth in the honored and divine Church of Christ: for he truly laid low the savagery of the idolaters, and, bestowing salvation, ever abideth with the faithful Wherefore, drawn by love, O mortals, let us now call him blessed, honoring the precious and glorious memory of the spiritual athlete, and crying aloud: O all-blessed Sozon, entreat Christ God on behalf of us all!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos of the holy martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Saved by faith, O much-suffering Sozon, thou art become a refuge for the tempest-tossed through the providence of Christ God; for pouring forth rivers of healings upon those who honor thee, thou dost ever drive out sickness and fever. Wherefore, we honor thy divine memory with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (martyr)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Go thou quickly before ...`,tone:4},{text:`Let heaven rejoice and let the earth be glad! For the heaven of God is born on earth: the divine Bride born of the promise. A barren woman nourisheth the babe Mary, and Joachim rejoiceth in her nativity, saying: The rod is born to me, from whence Christ, the Flower, hath arisen from the root of David! Truly this is a most glorious wonder!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (forefeast)`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`of_the_feast`],saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn of the forefeast, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`That which was mystically ordained ...`,tone:8}],kontakia_ode6:[{text:`Today Mary, the Virgin and Theotokos, * the boundless chamber of the heavenly Bridegroom, is born! * From a barren woman, by the counsel of God, * the chariot of the Word is rightly adorned; ** for she was foretold as the divine portal and Mother of life.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Kontakion of the forefeast (after Ode VI)`},label:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the forefeast, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},{text:`The divine maiden Mary, whom once the prophets of God foresaw in the Spirit, hath been given as the fruit of a barren woman. Beholding her today leaping up in the womb of Anna, with the faithful Joachim we noetically make haste to the appointed feast, and, standing afar off, cry aloud, saying: The restoration of this world hath now sprouted forth from the womb of the barren woman: the divine portal and Mother of life!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ikos of the forefeast`},label:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`Armed with the weapon of thy precious Cross, O Word, Thy spiritual athlete soundly vanquished the hosts of the adversary and put the tyrants to shame; he suffered for Thee, O my Christ, King of all, and ever reigneth with Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p11 Exapostilarion of the holy martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy martyr`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Be renewed, O Adam, and be thou magnified, O Eve! Ye prophets, join chorus with the apostles and the righteous! For the common joy of angels and mortals hath shone forth today from the righteous Joachim and Anna: Mary the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Exapostilarion of the forefeast`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Exapostilarion of the forefeast`},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the forefeast, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Come, ye descendants of Adam, * let us hymn the Virgin, * the most pure Mary, * who hath sprung forth from David ** and given birth to Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Let us offer praise * unto our Redeemer and Lord * Who from a barren woman * hath given us the Theotokos, ** the only Ever-virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`The rich among the people * shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The Mother of the King of all, * the joy of all the universe, * is born today * from a barren womb ** most gloriously.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`forefeast`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`The Queen of all, the dwelling-place of God who was foretold of old, the divine habitation of the ever-existent Essence, hath come forth today from the barren womb of the glorious Anna. Because of her, Hades hath been trampled underfoot, and Eve, the mother of us all, hath been led into steadfast life. Let us cry out to her as is meet: Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the Fruit of thy womb!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p12 Matins Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone II`,tone:2}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparia`,`kontakia`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of the canon of the forefeast, and 4 from ODE VI of the canon of the holy martyr.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`A fertile land is born from a barren land, bearing as fruit the Husbandman of all good things, the life-bearing Grain Who nourisheth all by His divine providence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Today hath the rod of virginity sprouted forth, from whence our God, the Gardener, hath blossomed forth as a flower, cutting down the branches of wickedness by His extreme beauty.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Lo! the mountain unquarried, which arose from a barren rock, produceth the noetically quarried Stone, Who crusheth the delusion of all graven idols.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring to be slain as an unblemished sacrifice, for the sake of God’s love, thou didst offer thyself up on His altar. Wherefore, we piously honor thee, O all-famed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having sailed over the deep of deception without foundering, thou didst attain unto the calm haven of the kingdom on high, O blessed martyr, enjoying everlasting quietude.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`The tormenter pitilessly raked thy sides with claws of iron; but thou didst gloriously commit thy spirit into the hands of God, O ever memorable and all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`O wonder more recent than all wonders! The Virgin conceived in her womb, without knowing a man, Him Who sustaineth all things, yet did not confine Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],troparia:[{text:`In his sufferings, Thy martyr Sozon O Lord, * received an imperishable crown from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * he set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By his supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Troparion of the holy martyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Mary, the divine maiden, is born unto us today * from the root of Jesse and the loins of David; * and all things rejoice and are made new through joy. * Rejoice together, O heaven and earth! * Praise her, ye lands of the gentiles! * Joachim maketh glad, and Anna holdeth festival, crying aloud: ** A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the Nourisher of our Life!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Troparion of the forefeast at Liturgy`},label:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the forefeast, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],kontakia:[{text:`Assembling today, with a loud voice let us praise Sozon, * the true and divinely wise martyr, * the skilled spiritual athlete of piety, * the initiate of the mysteries of grace, * the most generous bestower of healings: * for he entreateth Christ God ** on behalf of us all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p13 Kontakion of the holy martyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Sozon`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyr, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`Today Mary, the Virgin and Theotokos, * the boundless chamber of the heavenly Bridegroom, is born! * From a barren woman, by the counsel of God, * the chariot of the Word is rightly adorned; ** for she was foretold as the divine portal and Mother of life.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Kontakion of the forefeast at Liturgy`},label:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the forefeast, in Tone III`,tone:3}],prokeimenon:{text:`The righteous man shall be glad in the Lord, * and shall hope in Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O God, unto my prayer, when I make supplication unto Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE EPHESIANS,`,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§ 233 (Eph. 6: 10-17)`,citation:{book:`Ephesians`,chapter:6,verses:`10-17`,pericope_number:233},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The righteous cried, and the Lord heard them, and He delivered them out of all their tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},alleluia_verse:{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, and the Lord shall deliver them out of them all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO JOHN,`,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p14 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 52 (JN. 15: 17-16: 2)`,citation:{book:`John`,chapter:15,verses:`15:17-16:2`,pericope_number:52},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-07.pdf`,locus:`p15 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"09-08":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.little_vespers`,`c0.great_vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.great_vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`feast`,feast_ref:`nativity_theotokos`,title:{text:`THE NATIVITY OF OUR MOST HOLY SOVEREIGN LADY, THE THEOTOKOS AND EVER-VIRGIN MARY`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 8th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`great_feast`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`09-08.pdf`,note:'OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). Great Feast of the Theotokos; ODS 3rd ed. vol. III has no entry for 8 September (index checked). Fekula 2F names the Nativity (Sept. 8) among the feasts of the Theotokos it covers; rank and section as V1. Little Vespers; Great Vespers with 8 stichera (three of Sergius, the third "(Twice)"; three of Stephen of Jerusalem, the first "(Twice)"), three lessons, Litiya, blessing of the loaves; Matins with two canons (John of Damascus, Tone II; Andrew of Crete, Tone VIII), interleaved, stored whole. Canon II closes each ode with a Triadicon and a Theotokion. Ode IX: a rubric and refrain before each irmos (`preface`); no refrain is printed between the troparia here, unlike 21 November. ONE katavasia is printed before Ode IX, after Ode VII; after Ode IX the page gives "As Katavasia ... both Irmoi of ODE IX of the canon of the Exaltation of the Cross", stored in `closing`. The three lessons print no reference; citations are V1\'s identifications. The kontakion is pointed differently at its Liturgy site (final "**") and stored there as `liturgy_kontakion`. The Ode IX heading prints "OODE IX".',troparion:{text:`Thy nativity, O Virgin Theotokos, * hath proclaimed joy to all the world; * for from thee hath shone forth Christ our God, the Sun of righteousness, * Who, having annulled the curse, hath given His blessing, ** and having abolished death, hath granted us life everlasting.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the feast`},sourceLabel:`Troparion of the feast, in Tone IV`,tone:4,verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 Little Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p6 blessing of the loaves`,tone:4,repeat:3},{locus:`p7 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:3},{locus:`p18 after the Great Doxology`,tone:4},{locus:`p19 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}]},kontakion:{text:`In thy holy nativity, O most pure one, * Joachim and Anna have been freed from the reproach of childlessness, * and Adam and Eve from mortal corruption. * And, delivered from the affliction of sin, * thy people celebrate it, crying out to thee: * A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, * the nurturer of our Life!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Kontakion of the feast`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p13 after Ode VI`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the feast, in Tone IV`,tone:4},ikos:{text:`The supplication of Joachim over his childlessness, together with the sighing of Anna over her barrenness, were right acceptable to God: they entered the ears of the Lord and brought forth life-bearing fruit for the world. For the one made supplication on the mountain, and the other bore her reproach in the garden; and with joy the barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the nurturer of our Life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera of the feast, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Joachim and Anna hold festival, * having given birth to the only Theotokos, * the beginning of our salvation; * and with them we also celebrate today, * blessing the pure Virgin ** who sprang forth from the root of Jesse.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Today the Theotokos hath sprung forth * from Anna as a flower, a divinely wrought garden, * the salvation of mankind; * and in His beneficence the Creator of all, * Who was born of her in a manner past understanding, ** washeth away all the defilement of Adam, in that He is good.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Who is sufficiently worthy * to hymn the Virgin * who ineffably became a babe through Anna? * Ye mountains and hills, therefore, let sweetness fall today; * for the pure Theotokos, the life and cleansing of all, ** is nourished on milk.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`She who before was as a barren land * giveth birth to fertile ground, * and, having given forth a holy fruit from her fruitless womb, * she nurtureth her with milk. * O awesome wonder! The nurturer of our Life, ** who received the Bread of heaven in her womb is nourished with milk at her mother’s breasts!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],lic_closer:{text:`O most holy and pure Virgin, the multitude of angels in heaven, and we, the race of mankind on earth, bless thy most honored nativity, for thou hast become the Mother of Christ God, the Creator of all. We pray thee: cease not to beseech Him on behalf of us who after God, have set our hope on thee, O most hymned Theotokos who knewest not wedlock.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone IV`,tone:4},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the feast, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Rejoice, O Joachim and Anna! * Rejoice, for the Virgin, * the Mediatress of joy and salvation * is born unto us ** from a barren woman!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and Incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thou alone hast been shown to be * the salvation of mortals, * having given birth to the Word * in a manner transcending discourse and nature. ** Wherefore, we call thee blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`The rich among the people * shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Put away all grief, * O Adam and Eve; * for the Mother of Joy * springeth forth today most gloriously ** from a barren woman.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`The temple of God, * the only Theotokos, * doth issue forth * from a barren woman who hath not given birth; ** and Adam rejoiceth, crying aloud.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone II`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`,tone:2}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera of the feast, the composition of Sergius the Patriarch, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Today God, Who resteth on noetic thrones, hath prepared for Himself a holy throne on earth. He Who hath established the heavens by His wisdom hath in His loving-kindness created an animate heaven. For the God of wonders, the Hope of the hopeless, hath caused His Mother to spring forth as a Life-bearing plant from a barren root. Glory be to Thee, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,composer:`Sergius the Patriarch`,tone:6},{text:`This is the day of the Lord! Rejoice, O ye people! For lo! the bridal-chamber of the Light and the book of the Word of life hath issued forth from the womb, and the portal which faceth toward the east, having been born, awaiteth the entry of the great High Priest. She alone hath led the one Christ into the world, for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,composer:`Sergius the Patriarch`},{text:`Even though, by the will of God, famous barren women have produced offspring, yet in divine majesty hath Mary outshone all who have been born; for, having been most gloriously born of a barren mother, she supra-naturally gave birth in the flesh to the God of all, from a womb which knew not seed. She alone is the gate of the only-begotten Son of God; and He, passing through it, hath kept it closed, and, arranging all things wisely in accordance with His knowledge, hath wrought salvation for all mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,composer:`Sergius the Patriarch`,repeat:2},{text:`Today the gateway of the barren woman hath been opened, and the divine Virgin portal cometh forth! Today grace beginneth to bear fruit, revealing to the world the Mother of God, through whom those on earth are united to those in heaven, for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,composer:`Stephen of Jerusalem`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`The composition of Stephen of Jerusalem, in Tone VI`,tone:6},{text:`Today is the pronouncement of universal joy! Today the winds have blown which herald salvation, and our nature is released from barrenness! For the barren woman is shown to be the mother of her who remaineth virgin even after giving birth to the Creator, from whom God taketh upon Himself that which is alien to Him by nature, and Christ, the Redeemer of our souls, the Lover of mankind, doth accomplish salvation for the lost by means of flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,composer:`Stephen of Jerusalem`},{text:`Today barren Anna giveth birth to the divine maiden who was chosen beforehand out of all generations to be the dwelling-place of Christ our God, the King and Creator of all, in fulfillment of the divine dispensation. Thereby, O ye mortals, we have been fashioned anew and restored from corruption to endless life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,composer:`Stephen of Jerusalem`}],lic_closer:{text:`Today God, Who resteth on noetic thrones, hath prepared for Himself a holy throne on earth. He Who hath established the heavens by His wisdom hath in His loving-kindness created an animate heaven. For the God of wonders, the Hope of the hopeless, hath caused His Mother to spring forth as a Life-bearing plant from a barren root. Glory be to Thee, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM GENESIS`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Genesis`,chapter:28,verses:`10-17`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "Jacob went forth from the well of the oath"; closes "gate of heaven!" No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file, identified from the printed text; confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE PROPHECY OF EZEKIEL`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Ezekiel`,chapter:43,verses:`43:27-44:4`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "Thus saith the Lord: It shall come to pass from the eighth day". No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file, identified from the printed text; confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM PROVERBS`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:9,verses:`1-11`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Opens "Wisdom hath built a house for herself". No reference printed. Citation as V1 recorded it for this file, identified from the printed text; confirm the span against the page.`}],litiya:[{text:`Today is the beginning of our salvation, O ye people! For, lo! the Virgin Mother, who was foretold from generations of old as the receptacle of God, cometh forth to be born from a barren woman. The flower of Jesse and the rod of his root have sprung forth. Let Adam our forefather rejoice, and let Eve revel in jubilation! For, behold! She who was fashioned from the rib of Adam manifestly blesseth her daughter and descendant, saying: “Deliverance hath been born within me, for which cause I have been freed of the bonds of Hades!” Let David rejoice, striking his harp, and let him bless God: for, lo! the Virgin issueth forth from the womb of the barren woman, unto the salvation of our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,composer:`Stephen of Jerusalem`,sourceLabel:`At Litiya, these Stichera, the composition of Stephen of Jerusalem, in Tone I`,tone:1},{text:`Come, all ye who love virginity, ye zealots of purity! Come, and with love take up the praise of the Virgin: the well-spring of Life which floweth from the hardened stone, the bush which grew from the barren ground, unconsumed by the immaterial Fire, which purifieth and illumineth our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 2`},label:`plain`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`In Tone II`,label_inline:!0},{text:`What is this noise of revelers? Joachim and Anna keep festival mystically, saying: “Rejoice with us today, O Adam and Eve!” For by their transgression paradise was shut, but a right glorious fruit hath now been granted unto us: Mary, the divine maiden, the fruit which openeth wide its gates unto all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 3`},label:`plain`,composer:`Anatolius the Patriarch`,sourceLabel:`The composition of Anatolius the Patriarch`},{text:`The Queen of all who hath been foretold, the habitation of God, the divine dwelling place of the eternal Essence, hath come forth today from the barren womb of the glorious Anna, and by her, shameless Hades hath been trampled underfoot, and Eve, the mother of our race, hath been led into everlasting life. To her do we cry out, as is meet: Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 4`},label:`plain`}],litiya_closer:{text:`On the most excellent day of our feast let us strike the spiritual harp; for the Mother of Life is born today from the seed of David, dispelling darkness: the renewal of Adam, the restoration of Eve, the Well-spring of incorruption, our release from corruption. Because of her we have been deified and delivered from death. And we, the faithful, cry out to her with Gabriel: Rejoice, thou who art full of grace, the Lord is with thee, granting us great mercy for thy sake!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,composer:`Sergius`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of Sergius, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the feast, by Germanus, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`The joy of the whole world hath shone forth upon us from the righteous Joachim and Anna: the most laudable Virgin who, because of her surpassing purity, hath become the animate temple of God and is known as the one true Theotokos. Through her prayers, O Christ God, send down peace upon the world and great mercy upon our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,composer:`Germanus`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`In accordance with the angel’s prophecy, thou didst issue forth from the righteous Joachim and Anna, as a most pure fruit, heaven and the throne of God, a receptacle of purity, heralding forth joy to all the world, O Virgin, mediatress of our life, removal of the curse, bestowal of blessing. Wherefore, on the feast of thy nativity, O divinely called Virgin, ask peace for the world and great mercy for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The rich among the people * shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Today let the barren and childless Anna clap her hands with splendor, let those on earth bear lamps, let kings leap for joy, let hierarchs be glad in blessing, and let all the world keep festival; for, behold, the Queen, the immaculate Bride of the Father, hath sprung forth from the root of Jesse. No longer will women bear children in grief, for Joy hath blossomed forth and Life shall live amongst mortals in the world. No longer will the offerings of Joachim be rejected, for the lamentation of Anna hath been changed to joy, and she saith: “Rejoice with me, all ye chosen Israel, for, lo! the Lord hath given me the animate palace of His divine glory, for our common gladness and joy, and the salvation of our souls!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Come, all ye faithful, let us make haste to the Virgin, for lo! she is born who was foreseen before the womb as the Mother of our God, the vessel of virginity, the rod of Aaron which sprang forth from the root of Jesse, the proclamation of the prophets, the offspring of the righteous Joachim and Anna! She is born, and with her the world hath been restored! She is born, and the Church adorneth herself in her majesty! She is the holy temple and receptacle of the Godhead, the vessel of virginity, the bridal chamber of the King, wherein was wrought the most glorious and perfect mystery of the ineffable union of the natures which have come together in Christ! And worshipping Him, we hymn the nativity of the all-immaculate Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,composer:`Sergius`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of Sergius, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the loaves, the Troparion of the feast, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Blessing of the loaves rubric`}}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric.closing_rubric`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the feast, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 God is the Lord rubric`}},sessional_1:[{text:`Cry aloud, O David! What hath God sworn unto thee? “That which He hath sworn unto me,” saith he, “hath already been fulfilled! He hath given me of the fruit of my loins the Virgin, from whom Christ the Creator is to be born: the new Adam, the King Who sitteth on my throne! And He Whose kingdom is invisible reigneth today! A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the nurturer of our Life!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 1 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],sessional_2:[{text:`Today is Mary, the divine maiden, born for us from the root of Jesse and the loins of David. All things rejoice with joy and are renewed. Rejoice together, O heaven and earth! Praise her, ye people of our native land! Joachim maketh merry, and Anna keepeth festival, crying aloud: A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, the nurturer of our Life!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Sessional 2 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify thee, O most holy Virgin, we honor thy holy parents, and we glorify thy most glorious nativity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Remember, O Lord, David and all his meekness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God. (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`Let heaven rejoice, and let the earth be glad! For the divine heaven, the Bride of God, hath been born on earth according to His promise. The barren woman giveth suck to Mary as a babe, and Joachim rejoiceth in her birth, saying: “Unto me hath been born the staff from whence Christ shall spring forth as a flower, from the root of David! Truly most glorious is this wonder!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`That which was mystically commanded ...`,tone:8},{text:`Be thou renewed, O Adam! Rejoice, O Eve! Make merry, O David! Be of good cheer, O Anna, for the Mother of thy Creator is born most gloriously! All the earth joineth chorus, renewed, and rejoicing, clad in the vesture of gladness. Let every tongue now cry out to thee, O Mary, in chorus: Blessed is the house of David, for it nurtureth her who nourisheth our Life!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Polyeleos sessional Glory/Both now`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`I shall commemorate thy name * in every generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE,`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 4 (LK. 1: 39-49, 56)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:1,verses:`39-49, 56`,pericope_number:4},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`This is the day of the Lord! Rejoice, O ye people! For, lo! the bridal-chamber of the Light and the book of the Word of life hath issued forth from the womb, and the portal which faceth toward the east, having been born, awaiteth the entry of the great High Priest. She alone leadeth the one Christ into the world, for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone VI`,tone:6},canon_rubric:{text:`Two canons of the feast, with a total of 12 Troparia, each Irmos being chanted twice`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon I of the feast, the composition of John of Damascus, in Tone II:`,composer:`John of Damascus`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Come, O ye people, * let us sing a song to Christ our God, * Who divided the sea, * and made a way for the nation * which He had brought up out of the bondage of Egypt; * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Come ye faithful and rejoicing with divine spirit, let us honor with hymns the Ever-virgin maiden who today hath issued forth from a barren woman for the salvation of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O pure one, Mother and handmaid of Christ God, mediatress of our primal blessedness! All of us, the race of mankind, glorify thee with hymns, as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today the bridge of life is born, through which mortals have attained restoration after their fall into Hades, glorifying Christ, the Bestower of life, with hymns.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, who didst slay sin upon the Tree, * firmly establish us in Thee, * and in the hearts of us who hymn Thee * plant the fear of Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having lived blamelessly for God, ye gave birth unto the salvation of all, O divinely wise parents of her who hath given birth to our Creator and God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`From a barren woman did the Lord, Who poureth forth life upon all, cause the Virgin to come forth, in whom He was pleased to make His abode, preserving her incorrupt even after giving birth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us hymn Mary today as the Theotokos, the fruit of Anna, the intercessor and helper of all, who gaveth birth to the life-bearing Cluster.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard report of Thy dispensation, O Lord, * and have glorified Thee * Who alone lovest mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`We hymn Thee, O Lord, Who hast given unto all, as a haven of salvation, her who gaveth birth to Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ hath revealed thee, O Bride of God, to all who with faith hymn thy mystery as their boast and might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Delivered from transgressions by thy supplications, O Lady who knewest not wedlock, we all bless thee with a good and proper understanding.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Having destroyed the darkness of shadowy images * and illumined the hearts of the faithful * by the coming of Truth through the divine maiden, O Christ, * do Thou guide us by Thy light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ye people, let us hymn the cause of the Cause of all that is, Who became like unto us. For the prophets, deemed worthy to behold her image, rejoiced, clearly seeing the fruit of salvation brought forth through her.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The sprouting of the dry rod of the priest showed forth the destiny of Israel; and now the all-glorious offspring of the barren woman most gloriously shineth forth the splendor of those who gave birth to her.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`From within the sea monster Jonah cried unto the Lord: * “Lead me up from the abyss of Hades, I pray Thee; * for with a voice of praise as to my Redeemer, * in the spirit of truth * I offer myself to Thee.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The divinely wise parents of the Mother of God cried out to the Lord in grief over their barrenness; but they have now given birth to her, our common boast and salvation for generations of generations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The divinely wise parents of the Mother of God received a gift worthy of heaven from God, for she is a chariot more highly exalted than the cherubim, the Mother of the Word and Creator.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The bush which burned with fire on the mountain * and the dew-bearing furnace of the Chaldeans * clearly prefigured thee, O Bride of God; * for, without being consumed, * thou didst receive the divine and immaterial Fire * within thy material womb. * Wherefore, we chant unto Him Who was born of thee: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Once, the transmitter of the law was prevented from understanding thy great mystery in material manifestations, O most pure one, though instructed through images to not think earthly thoughts. Wherefore, marveling at the wonder, he said: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In a godly manner the divine choir called thee beforehand the mountain and portal of heaven and the noetic ladder; for from thee was the Stone cut without the aid of the hands of man, and thou art the door through which passed the Lord of wonders, the God of our fathers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Of old in the furnace of the holy children, * Thou didst prefigure Thy Mother, O Lord, * in the image of those who entered therein, * and rescued therefrom remained unconsumed. * Her who hath been revealed today do we hymn * unto the ends of the earth, * supremely exalting her throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Now the designated tabernacle of our reconciliation to God, who is to give birth to the Word Who hath revealed Himself to us in the coarseness of our flesh, beginneth her existence. Him do we, who have been brought into existence out of non-existence, hymn and supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The reversal of Anna’s barrenness hath loosed the world’s lack of good things, and hath plainly shown forth a miracle: Christ, Who hath come to mortal men. Him do we, who have been brought into existence out of non-existence, hymn and supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},9:{preface:[{text:`At ODE IX we do not sing the Magnificat, we chant before the Irmos and before each of the Troparia of Canon I, this refrain:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon I preface rubric`},label:`rubric`},{text:`Magnify, O my soul, the most glorious nativity of the Mother of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon I preface refrain`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Refrain`,label_inline:!0}],irmos:{text:`Thee do we magnify, O blessed and all-pure Theotokos, * who through thy virginal womb ineffably brought forth * God incarnate, * the Luminary Who shone forth before the sun * and hath come to us in the flesh.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He Who poured forth water from the stone for the rebellious people, through the womb of a barren woman hath given to us, the right submissive nations, the fruit of gladness: thee, O most pure Mother of God, whom we magnify as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon I 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thee, O Theotokos, do we magnify, who hast removed the ancient and precipitous condemnation: the restoration of our first mother, the cause of the reconciliation of our race to God, the bridge to the Creator.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon I 2`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon II of the feast, the composition of Andrew of Crete, in Tone VIII:`,composer:`Andrew of Crete`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`To Him who crushed the enemy with His arm * and led Israel through the Red Sea, * to our Redeemer and our God let us sing, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Let all creation join chorus, and let David be glad, for from his tribe and seed hath come forth the rod which beareth the Lord, the Creator of all, as a flower.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`She who is holy among the saints is placed in the holy sanctuary as a babe, to be fed by the hands of angels. Let us all, therefore, faithfully keep festival together on her nativity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Anna was barren and unable to give birth, yet she was not childless in God’s eyes; for, lo! she hath become known by all generations as the mother of the pure Virgin, from whom the Creator of nature hath sprung forth in the guise of a servant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`With hymns we all honor thee, the innocent ewe-lamb who hast been born of Anna and who through thy womb brought Christ the Lamb into our nature.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`I glorify the three Beginningless Ones, I hymn the three Holy Ones, I proclaim the three equally Everlasting Ones to be of a single Essence; for the one God is glorified in the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Who hath seen a Babe fed with milk Whom a father hath now sown? Or where hath there been seen a Mother who is a Virgin? Truly past understanding are both of these things, O pure Birthgiver of God. Katavasia: Inscribing the invincible weapon of the Cross upon the waters, * Moses marked a straight line before him with his staff * and divided the Red Sea, * opening a path for Israel who went over dry-shod. * Then he marked a second line across the waters * and united them in one, * overwhelming the chariots of Pharaoh. * Therefore let us sing to Christ our God, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`My heart is established in the Lord, * my horn is exalted in my God, * my mouth is enlarged against mine enemies, * and I rejoice in Thy salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Blessed is thy womb, O chaste Anna, for thou didst pour forth the fruit of virginity, who gaveth birth without seed to Jesus the Redeemer the Nurturer of creation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Ever-virgin, all creation calleth thee blessed who hast been born today of Anna as the rod sprung forth from the root of Jesse, who put forth Christ as a most pure Bloom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Showing thee to be more exalted than all creation, O pure Theotokos, thy Son magnifieth thy birth from Anna, gladdening all today.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We worship Thee, O Father, beginningless in essence, we hymn Thy timeless Son, and we honor Thy Spirit Who is equally everlasting: as God three in Hypostases but one in Essence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O pure Birthgiver of God, who hast given birth unto the Bestower of light, the Author of man’s life, thou hast been revealed to be the treasure of our life and the portal of the unapproachable Light. Katavasia: The rod of Aaron is an image of this mystery, * for when it budded it showed who should be priest. * So in the Church, that once was barren, * the wood of the Cross hath now budded forth, * filling her with strength and steadfastness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`With noetic eyes the prophet Habbakuk * foresaw Thy coming, O Lord; * wherefore he cried aloud: * ‘God shall come out of Theman!’ Glory to Thy power! * Glory to Thy condescension!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The Patriarch Jacob, clearly foreseeing the mighty works of Thy dispensation, O Savior, cried out in the Spirit, saying mystically to Judah: “From the tender plant thou art gone up, O my Son!”, referring to Thee, O God, Who wast born of the Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Now the pure Virgin, the rod of Aaron which sprung forth from the root of David, cometh forth from Anna, and heaven and earth, and all the nations of the gentiles mystically join chorus together with Anna and Joachim.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let heaven now be glad; let the earth rejoice! And let Joachim and David join chorus: the one as the father of thee who truly hast given birth to God, and the other as thine ancestor who proclaimed thy mighty deeds, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The whole world rejoiceth with thee today, O divinely wise Anna; for thou hast budded forth the Mother of its Redeemer, she who from the root of David put forth for us the rod of strength which beareth Christ as a flower.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`I glorify God, the beginningless Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit, the consubstantial, uncreated Trinity, before Whom, the seraphim stand with reverence, crying aloud: Holy, Holy, Holy art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The beginningless Origin receiveth a beginning from thee in the flesh and in time, O Theotokos, and He remaineth equally the beginningless and incarnate Word of the Father, equally everlasting with the Spirit, maintaining His divine dignity. Katavasia: O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation; * I have considered Thy works, * and I have glorified Thy Divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Lord our God, bestow Thy peace upon us; * O Lord our God, take us for Thy possession; * O Lord, besides Thee we know none other: * and we call upon Thy Name.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy nativity is most pure, O immaculate Virgin, thy conception is ineffable, and thy birthgiving unutterable, O Bride unwedded; for God hath clothed Himself in all of me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let the angelic ranks be glad; let the descendants of Adam join chorus; for the rod who alone budded forth the Flower Christ, our Redeemer, hath been born.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today the condemnation of Eve hath been lifted by thy nativity, the barrenness of Anna hath been loosed, and Adam hath been freed from the ancient curse; for by thee have we been delivered from corruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Glory to Thee Who hast glorified the barren woman today! For, according to the promise, she hath given birth to the flowering rod from whence Christ, the Flower of our life, hath budded forth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Glory to Thee, O holy Father, unbegotten God! Glory to Thee, O timeless and only-begotten Son! Glory to Thee, O Spirit divine and co-enthroned, Who proceedest from the Father and restest in the Son!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thy womb became the chariot of the Sun; thy purity remained intact as before, O Virgin; for Christ the Sun hath appeared from thee like a Bridegroom from a bridal chamber. Katavasia: O thrice-blessed Tree, on which Christ the king and Lord was stretched! * Through thee the beguiler fell, * who tempted mankind with the tree. * He was caught in the trap set by God, * who was crucified upon thee in the flesh, * granting peace unto our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The billows of life trouble me like the waters of the sea, * O Lover of Mankind. * Wherefore, like Jonah I cry unto Thee, O Word: * Raise up my life from corruption, O compassionate Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`We hymn thy holy nativity and honor thine immaculate conception of Christ, O divinely chosen Bride and Virgin. And with us the ranks of angels and the souls of the saints glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy chaste parents placed thee, who art holy among the saints, in the temple of the Lord, O pure one, to be raised with honor in preparation to become His Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Join chorus, ye barren women and mothers! Be of good cheer and leap up, O ye childless! For a childless and barren woman hath budded forth the Theotokos who delivereth Eve from her birth pangs and Adam from the curse.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I hearken to David who singeth to thee: The virgins that follow after thee shall be brought into the temple of the King. And with him I also hymn thee, the daughter of the King.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thee, O pure one, is the mystery of the Trinity hymned and glorified; for well pleased was the Father to have the Word make His abode within thee, and the divine Spirit to overshadow thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thou wast a golden candlestick, O pure Birthgiver of God, for in thy womb the Fire made His abode: the Word from the Holy Spirit; and He became visible in thee in human form. Katavasia: Jonah stretched out his hands in the form of a cross * within the belly of the sea monster, * plainly prefiguring the redeeming Passion. * Cast out from thence after three days, * he foreshadowed the marvelous Resurrection of Christ our God, * who was crucified in the flesh and enlightened the world * by His Rising on the third day.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The Chaldean furnace, burning with fire, * was bedewed by the Spirit * through the presence of God; * and the children chanted: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`We celebrate and bow down with faith before thy holy nativity, O pure one, honoring thy Son, by Whom we have now been delivered from the ancient condemnation of Adam.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Now Anna maketh merry and, rendering praise, crieth aloud: Though barren, I have given birth unto the Mother of God, for whose sake the condemnation of Eve, the travail of birthgiving, hath been loosed!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adam hath been freed and Eve danceth; and they cry out to thee in spirit, O Theotokos: Through thee have we been delivered from the primeval curse by the appearance of Christ!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O the womb which contained the dwelling place of God! O the womb which bore her who is more spacious than the heavens, the holy throne, the noetic ark of sanctification!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`We glorify-the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit in the unity of the Godhead, the most holy Trinity, indivisible, uncreated, equally everlasting and consubstantial.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Most gloriously didst thou alone give birth unto God, O Virgin. By thy nativity thou hast renewed nature, O Mary. Thou hast released Eve from the primeval curse, O pure Birthgiver of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The senseless decree of the wicked tyrant, * breathing forth threats and blasphemy hateful to God, * confused the people. * Yet neither the fury of the wild beast nor the roaring of the fire * could frighten the three children: * but standing together in the flame, * fanned by the wind that brought the dew as refreshment, they sang: * ‘Blessed and supremely praised art Thou, * O our God and the God of our fathers.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 7 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},8:{irmos:{text:`O Thou who dost cover Thy chambers on high with the waters, * Thou Who hast set the sands to bound the sea * and Who upholdest all things: * the sun doth sing Thy praises, * the moon giveth Thee glory, * every creature offereth a hymn unto Thee, * as their Fashioner, throughout the ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou, O holy God, Who wrought most glorious things through the barren womb, Who opened the childless womb of Anna and gave her fruit, and Thou, O Son of the Virgin, didst receive flesh from her, the ever-flourishing Virgin and Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou, O Lord, Who dost close the abyss and open it, Who dost raise water to the clouds and give rain, hast granted the holy Anna to bud forth and give birth unto the most pure fruit, the Theotokos, from a barren root.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Cultivator of our thoughts, Planter of our souls, Who hast shown forth the barren earth to be right fruitful, hast made the holy Anna, a field which before was barren, to become plentiful, right fertile and fruitful, giving rise to the Theotokos, the most pure fruit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come ye all, let us gaze upon the city of God born as if from a little chamber, issuing forth from the gate of Anna’s womb, yet lacking in any knowledge of the path of intercourse, for the one God and Creator hath issued forth via this strange path.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O transcendent Trinity, beginningless Unity, the multitude of angels hymneth and trembleth before Thee; heaven and earth are in awe of Thee; men bless Thee, and fire doth serve Thee in obedience. Everything in creation doth submit to Thee with fear, O holy Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 8 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O report most new! God hath become the Son of a woman! O seedless birthgiving! O Mother without a husband, O begotten God! O awesome sight! O, the strange conception of the Virgin! O the ineffable nativity, truly past all understanding and contemplation! Katavasia: O children equal in number to the Trinity: * bless ye God, the Father and Creator; * hymn ye the Word Who came down * and transformed the fire into dew; * and supremely exalt ye Him Who giveth life unto all, * the all-holy Spirit, * throughout the ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Virginity is alien to motherhood, * and childbearing is a thing strange to virgins: * yet in thee, O Theotokos, both have come to pass. * Therefore we, and all the nations of the earth, * without ceasing call thee blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast received a nativity worthy of thy purity, O Mother of God; for, according to the promise, thou wast given to the barren one as a fruit divinely springing forth. Wherefore, all we, the peoples of the earth, unceasingly magnify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`I shall raise up the tabernacle of sacred David which hath fallen, which was a fore-type of thee, O pure one, through whom the dust of all mankind hath been fashioned into a body for God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`We venerate thy swaddling clothes, O Theotokos. We glorify Him Who gaveth fruit to her who before was barren, and Who most gloriously opened the womb of her who was unable to give birth. For as God, He doeth all things whatsoever He desireth with complete authority.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`To thee, O Theotokos who wast born of Anna, do we faithfully offer up hymnody as a gift, mothers and virgins glorifying thee as the only Mother and Virgin; and we bow down before thee and hymn and glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`It is foreign for the iniquitous to glorify the beginningless Trinity: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit, the uncreated omnipotent Principle, by Whom the whole world is held fast at the behest of His might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Within thy womb, O Mother, thou didst contain One of the Trinity: Christ the King, Whom all creation doth hymn and before Whom the ranks of heaven tremble. Him do thou entreat, O all-pure one, that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],preface:[{text:`Before the Irmos and Troparia of Canon II, we chant this refrain:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon II preface rubric`},label:`rubric`},{text:`Magnify, O my soul, the Virgin Mary who hath been born of the barren woman!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 9 Canon II preface refrain`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Refrain`,label_inline:!0}],closing:[{text:`As Katavasia, we chant here both Irmoi of ODE IX of the canon of the Exaltation of the Cross:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 katavasia rubric`},label:`rubric`},{text:`O Theotokos, thou art a mystical Paradise, * who untilled brought forth Christ. * by Whom the life-giving Tree of the Cross hath been planted upon the earth: * Therefore celebrating its exaltation on this day, * Him do we worship * and thee do we magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 Katavasia I`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Katavasia I`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Today the death that came to man through eating of the tree, * is made of no effect through the Cross. * For the curse of our Mother Eve * that fell on all mankind * is destroyed by the fruit of the pure Mother of God, * whom all the powers of heaven magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 Katavasia II`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Katavasia II`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Like a cloud of light the Virgin Mary, the Theotokos, hath truly shone forth upon us today, coming forth from the righteous ones for our glory. No longer is Adam condemned, and Eve hath been freed from her bonds. Wherefore, we exclaim, crying aloud with boldness to her who alone is pure: Thy nativity doth announce joy to the whole world!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the feast, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode III sessional repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],exapostilarion:{text:`Today the Theotokos doth issue forth like a flower from the barren Anna, instilling all the ends of the world with a most divine fragrance, filling all creation with joy. Hymning her, we praise her as is meet, as the one who is more exalted than all those earthborn.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the feast`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Be thou renewed, O Adam! Be thou magnified, O Eve! Join ye chorus with the apostles and the righteous! For Mary the Theotokos, the common joy of the angels and mortals, hath shone forth today from the righteous Joachim and Anna.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p17 Exapostilarion Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ...,`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the feast, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`O wondrous miracle! The well-spring of Life is born of the barren woman, and grace doth splendidly begin to bring forth fruit. Be glad, O Joachim, as thou art the father of the Theotokos! There is none to compare with thee among mortal parents, O God-pleaser! For the maiden who contained God, the divine dwelling place, the most holy mountain, hath been given to us by thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`O wondrous marvel! ...`},{text:`O wondrous miracle! Fruit hath shone forth from the barren woman at the behest of the Almighty Creator of all. She hath boldly loosed the barrenness of the world. Ye mothers, join chorus with the mother of the Theotokos, crying: O joyous one, rejoice! The Lord is with thee, Who through thee granteth the world great mercy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O wondrous marvel! ...`},{text:`The right glorious Anna, who hath been revealed to be an animate pillar of chastity, a splendid receptacle resplendent with grace, hath truly given birth to the bulwark of virginity, the divine flower who manifestly imparteth the beauty of virginity to all the virginal who desire to preserve the gift of virginity, and bestoweth great mercy upon all the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O wondrous marvel! ...`}],praises_closer:{text:`This is the day of the Lord! Rejoice, O ye people! For, lo! the bridal-chamber of the Light and the book of the Word of life hath issued forth from the womb, and the portal which faceth toward the east, having been born, awaiteth the entry of the great High Priest. She alone leadeth the one Christ into the world, for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Praises Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology. Troparion, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Great Doxology. Troparion`}},closing_rubric:{text:`Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p18 Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`liturgy_kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`megalynarion_rubric`,`megalynarion_refrain`,`megalynarion`,`megalynarion_closing_rubric`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of Canon I of the feast, and 4 from ODE VI of Canon II of the feast.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitudes rubric`}},liturgy_kontakion:{text:`In thy holy nativity, O most pure one, * Joachim and Anna have been freed from the reproach of childlessness, * and Adam and Eve from mortal corruption. * And, delivered from the affliction of sin, * thy people celebrate it, crying out to thee: * A barren woman giveth birth to the Theotokos, ** the nurturer of our Life!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Kontakion at Liturgy`},sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the feast, in Tone IV`,tone:4},beatitudes:[{text:`Having lived blamelessly for God, ye gave birth unto the salvation of all, O divinely wise parents of her who hath given birth to our Creator and God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`From a barren woman did the Lord, Who poureth forth life upon all, cause the Virgin to come forth, in whom He was pleased to make His abode, preserving her incorrupt even after giving birth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us hymn Mary today as the Theotokos, the fruit of Anna, the intercessor and helper of all, who gaveth birth to the life-bearing Cluster.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We hymn thy holy nativity and honor thine immaculate conception of Christ, O divinely chosen Bride and Virgin. And with us the ranks of angels and the souls of the saints glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy chaste parents placed thee, who art holy among the saints, in the temple of the Lord, O pure one, to be raised with honor in preparation to become His Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thee, O pure one, is the mystery of the Trinity hymned and glorified; for well pleased was the Father to have the Word make His abode within thee, and the divine Spirit to overshadow thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude Glory ...`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ...,`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thou wast a golden candlestick, O pure Birthgiver of God, for in thy womb the Fire made His abode: the Word from the Holy Spirit; and He became visible in thee in human form.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Beatitude Both now ...`},label:`both_now`,sourceLabel:`Both now ...,`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`My soul doth magnify the Lord, * and my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Savior.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},tone:3,sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone III: The hymn of the Theotokos`,label_inline:!0},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`For He hath looked upon the lowliness of His handmaiden; for behold, from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p19 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE PHILIPPIANS,`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§ 240 (PHIL. 2: 5-11)`,citation:{book:`Philippians`,chapter:2,verses:`5-11`,pericope_number:240},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, and incline thine ear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VIII`,label_inline:!0,tone:8},alleluia_verse:{text:`The rich among the people shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE,`,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 54 (LK. 10: 38-42; 11: 27-28)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:10,verses:`10:38-42, 11:27-28`,pericope_number:54},citation_basis:`printed`},megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Instead of “It is truly meet ...,” we chant the Irmos of ODE IX of Canon I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Instead of It is truly meet`}},megalynarion_refrain:{text:`Magnify, O my soul, the most glorious nativity of the Mother of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Refrain before the festal Irmos`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Refrain`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion:{text:`Thee do we magnify, O blessed and all-pure Theotokos, * who through thy virginal womb ineffably brought forth * God incarnate, * the Luminary Who shone forth before the sun * and hath come to us in the flesh.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Irmos of Ode IX of Canon I, at Liturgy`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`This is done until the leave-taking of the feast.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 until the leave-taking`}},communion_verse:{text:`I will take the cup of salvation, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08.pdf`,locus:`p20 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}},{kind:`feast`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE FINDING OF THE WONDERWORKING ICON OF THE MOST HOLY THEOTOKOS KNOWN AS THE KURSK-ROOT ICON OF THE SIGN`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 8th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`polyeleos`,fekula_section:`2E`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`09-08A.pdf`,note:'OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). Second file of 8 September, a separate service (the Finding of the Kursk-Root Icon), beside the Great Feast. RANK FOLLOWS V1: polyeleos, Fekula 2E. THE SAME PRINTED SERVICE appears again as 11-27A.pdf, which was stored `vigil` / 2F provisionally on its printed Litiya; ODS vol. III shows a printed Litiya does not settle Vigil against Polyeleos, and V1 took Polyeleos. The two entries must end up with one rank: open question Q-0002. Great Vespers with 8 stichera, three lessons, a Litiya; Polyeleos with a magnification; no blessing of the Loaves rubric, no Great Doxology rubric; Matins ends with the Praises. The first two Vespers lessons print no reference; the third prints "(9:1-11)". This file writes "Both now" where 11-27A writes "Now & ever".',troparion:{text:`Having acquired thee as an unassailable rampart * and a fount of miracles, * we, thy servants, set at naught armies of adversaries, * O most pure Theotokos. * Wherefore, do we entreat thee: * Grant peace to our native land ** and great mercy to our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Troparion of the holy icon`},sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy icon, in Tone IV`,tone:4,verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 end of Great Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p6 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:3},{locus:`p15 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}]},kontakion:{text:`Come, ye faithful, let us radiantly celebrate * the wondrous appearance of the most precious image of the Mother of God, * and drawing grace therefrom, * let us cry out with compunction: * Rejoice, O Theotokos, ** blessed Mary, Mother of God!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Kontakion of the holy icon`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p10 after Ode VI`,tone:6},{locus:`p15 AT LITURGY`,tone:6}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy icon, in Tone VI`,tone:6},ikos:{text:`Through thee, O Theotokos, the pre-eternal Word was made flesh; through thee men have beheld the Sun of righteousness, upon Whom the angels dare not gaze: for in thine arms was borne Him Whom the cherubim bear aloft, and by thy most pure hands was held the Almighty Creator of all. O daughter of mortal Adam, thou wast called the one who gaveth birth to God. Wherefore, as one who alone hath maternal boldness before Him, pause not in thy prayers for the whole world, lifting up thy God-pleasing hands to thy Son, and inclining His love for mankind towards thy servants who cry out to thee with thankful mouths: Rejoice, O Theotokos, blessed Mary, Mother of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10-p11 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya_rubric`,`litiya`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,”`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera; five in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O all-hymned Virgin, * immaculate Mother of God the Word, * the astonishment of angel, and help of Christians, * be thou unto us an unassailable wall * against the assaults of enemies, visible and invisible, * stretching forth unto thy Son thy hands which held God, * destroying by thine almighty supplication * the counsels of the impious, ** and revealing the sign of thy mercy unto us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`,tone:8},{text:`O Lady Theotokos, our hope unashamed, * bowing the knee of our hearts at this time, * we cry to thee in compunction: * The Russian land, which of old was called thy home, * do thou snatch from the hands of the devil, * stretching forth unto thy Son thy hands which held God, * by thy supplication * consuming all the dominion of the enemy, ** and revealing the sign of thy mercy unto us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O thou joy of all joys! * Most sweet consolation of those who sorrow! * Surety of sinners! * Salvation of the faithful * Lead us to the heavenly Kingdom, * compensating for our weaknesses by thine intercession; * intercede for us before the dread judgment seat of Christ, * delivering us from everlasting torment, ** and revealing the sign of thy mercy unto us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O wondrous tidings! * O most glorious sight! * An icon of the Theotokos hid within a grove, * and pouring forth a spring of living water * ever flowing to life eternal! * Wherefore, having found it, let us form a chorus, * and, clapping our hands with gladness, let us cry: * Rejoice, O most blessed one, ** for thou hast come unto us who are paupers!`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`Sanctified by the wood of the Cross, * the trees of the forest pay homage * to the immaculate Mother * of Him Who stretched forth His hands upon the Tree; * for they preserved * the image of thy most pure face, * that being wondrously discovered, * the Church might be robed in its comeliness, ** and the faithful may be partakers of divine grace.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O all ye generations of the earth, bless Mary the Theotokos: Ye righteous and sinners, form one choir for her; ye virgins, hymn the ever-Virgin, the boast of virginity; ye mothers, praise the Mother of our Creator and God; ye elders, bow down before her who gave flesh to the Ancient of Days; ye babes, glorify her who hath held the pre-eternal Infant in her arms; ye poor, magnify her who doth possess a wealth of mercy and grace; ye kings, exalt the Queen of heaven and earth; and kissing her precious image, let us cry aloud: Rejoice, O inexhaustible joy and salvation of our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`And these Stichera, in Tone III`,tone:3},{text:`O Lady, thy most precious icon hath appeared as a sign of thy good pleasure unto us, whereat, bending down as to a life-bearing spring, we draw forth the water of immortality, and freely receive divers healings; and worshiping thee, the prototype, we cry in faith: O most holy Theotokos, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC 7`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure Virgin: the light, joy and protection of our souls, thou art the estrangement from sorrows and remission of sins, the fulfillment of humble requests and ever-flowing fount of grace, O immaculate one. Wherefore, falling down before thee, we pray: Cease not to cry to thy Son and God for us, that being delivered by thee from misfortunes, we may obtain great mercy from Christ the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC 8`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`Forming a most festive choir today, come ye, let us hymn the Virgin Theotokos; and, kissing her most pure image, let us cry: O most holy Lady, deliver thine inheritance from cruel enemies, and strengthen the faithful in the doing of good, entreating thy Son and God for all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone I`,tone:1},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the Day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`READING FROM THE BOOK OF GENESIS`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Genesis`,chapter:28,verses:`10-17`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. The body opens "And Jacob went out from Beersheba" and closes "this is the gate of heaven": Genesis 28:10-17, as V1 identified it for this file. Confirm.`},{heading:`READING FROM THE BOOK OF THE PROPHET EZEKIEL`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Ezekiel`,chapter:43,verses:`43:27-44:4`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "And when these days are expired, it shall be", closes "I fell upon my face": Ezekiel 43:27-44:4, as V1 identified it for this file. Confirm.`},{heading:`READING FROM THE PROVERBS`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Lesson 3`},citation_verbatim:`(9:1-11)`,citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:9,verses:`1-11`},citation_basis:`printed`}],litiya_rubric:{text:`At the Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple, and these Stichera:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Litiya rubric`}},litiya:[{text:`Come, all ye peoples of our native land, let us hasten to the temple of the Lord; let us praise the all-hymned Mother of our God, and bow down before her most pure image in faith, for it hath now been given to the Russian land as a pledge of salvation. Wherefore, radiantly keeping the feast thereof, let us unceasingly cry out to the Theotokos: Rejoice, ready help of the world, thou joy and salvation of our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,sourceLabel:`In Tone I`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Laying aside all earthly care, and forsaking the vanity of the world, let us lift up our eyes unto the holy hill, from whence cometh our help; for lo! the Queen of heaven, standing at the right hand of her Son and God, doth pray without ceasing. Wherefore, let us, who have been delivered from misfortune by her intercessions, be glad, and say: Rejoice, our fervent helper, thou salvation of our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Litiya 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us be filled today with great joy, and giving thanks with compunction let us cry out in fear and trembling: Why is this granted to us, that the Mother of our God hath come to us? For lo! her healing icon abideth in our midst, and we dare to touch it, to bow down before it, to kiss it, and to offer entreaty to its prototype, as to one that is truly with us. Wherefore, marveling at her condescension, we cry: Rejoice, O Virgin Theotokos, full of grace!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Litiya 3`},label:`plain`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`In Tone II`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Come, all ye that labor and are heavy laden; come, ye who weep and mourn; come, ye who have lacked patience; come, ye poor and afflicted! Fall down before the icon of the most pure Virgin, and receive ye, each according to his need; for lo! the all-hymned Theotokos giveth all to each abundantly. She is the healing of the infirm, the most sweet consolation of those who grieve, the forgiveness of sinners and the salvation of all who have recourse to her in faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p3-p4 Litiya 4`},label:`plain`,tone:7,sourceLabel:`In Tone VII`,label_inline:!0}],litiya_closer:{text:`When the fullness of time shall come; when the trumpet of the archangel shall sound; then the thrones of judgment shall be set, and the rivers of fire shall make a fearsome noise; the dead will arise and the living shall be caught up, and the sign of the Son of man shall appear in heaven, all the inhabitants of the earth shall weep, and all the powers of heaven shall be shaken. Then shall the Virgin Theotokos, the salvation of sinners and hope of the hopeless, appear, standing at the right hand of the Judge, stretching forth her most pure hands to her Son, mercifully bedewing her cheeks with tears, and delivering from everlasting torment those who call upon her all-hymned name. Therefore, brethren, let us now make haste, and delay not in approaching the Theotokos, that she, upon whom we place all our hope, may help us at that dreadful hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the holy icon, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Truly thou pourest forth rivers of grace from thine icon, O Theotokos! For lo! even at the site of its discovery, a spring of healing water hath appeared. Thou dost quench the spiritual thirst of all who have recourse to thee in love, washing away sins, and granting us to draw forth joy and gladness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`At the root of a tree the image of her that budded forth the Tree of life was found. Wherefore, on the site of its appearance, a monastery was planted, like a spiritual orchard, wherein the all-hymned name of its prototype was glorified, supplications for the whole world were ceaselessly offered up, and men worked out their salvation with fear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord hath sworn in truth unto David, * and He will not annul it.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Having the warriors of heaven as aides, and the Virgin Theotokos as an invincible commander, let us array ourselves against the enemies of our salvation, armed with the precious Cross, crying out to the most blessed one: Deprive us not of thy mighty assistance, for we have placed our hope on thee, that we be not put to shame forever.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`O Virgin Theotokos, how much more powerful than the hands of Moses are thy most pure hands, ever raised to God on our behalf? Wherefore, thou dost vanquish an enemy more powerful than Amalek, routing the very prince of darkness and his minions, granting victory to those who piously war against the passions, and showing them forth as heirs of the new promised land, wherein righteousness doth dwell.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone V`,tone:5}},matins:{order:[`god_is_lord_rubric`,`troparion`,`sessional_1`,`sessional_2`,`megalynarion_rubric`,`megalynarion`,`megalynarion_verse_rubric`,`megalynarion_verse`,`sessional_polyeleos`,`anabathmoi_rubric`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`gospel_rubric`,`gospel`,`psalm50_sticheron`,`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`praises_rubric`,`praises`,`praises_closer`],god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the holy icon, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 God is the Lord rubric`}},sessional_1:[{text:`We are thy servants, O Theotokos, having abandoned our slavery to sin forever and bowed our necks beneath the easy yoke of Christ. Wherefore, we hope to obtain the freedom of the children of God by thy fervent intercession for us, that unceasingly rejoicing in thee we may cry to thy Son and our God: O our Savior, glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone V`,tone:5},{text:`Rejoice, thou who art robed with the sun and dost shine ineffably with glory! Rejoice, Mother of the Almighty, who hath revealed to the world the pre-eternal Word and who most gloriously crushed the head of the serpent, that by thy birthgiving the race of Adam hath been freed from corruption! Rejoice, thou who alone art ever-Virgin even after giving birth!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 1 Glory/Both now`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in the same tone`}],sessional_2:[{text:`O ye faithful, with one voice let us hymn today her who bestoweth the gifts of her mercy abundantly upon all in need, who taketh under her mighty protection all who flee unto her, and who in her maternal love doth embrace the wicked as well as the good. Wherefore, come, ye monks and layfolk, ye rich and poor, and forming one choir, let the Church of heaven and earth celebrate together, crying out with one voice to the Theotokos, and exclaiming: Rejoice, O thou who art full of grace, the Lord is with thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated..`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 2 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`After the Polyeleos, this Magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`Meet it is to magnify thee, O Theotokos, that art more honorable than the cherubim and beyond compare more glorious than the seraphim.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`O God, give Thy judgment to the king, and thy righteousness to the son of the king.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`The most radiant feast of the Theotokos is at hand today, whereon the spiritual light of the world hath shone forth in her nativity, and wherein a great treasure hath been given to our land in the appearance of the most glorious icon of the Theotokos, bowing down before whom with fear we now cry aloud: Rejoice, O Virgin, thou salvation of the faithful!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Then, the Sessional Hymn of the holy icon, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Polyeleos sessional repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`The Song of Ascents, the first Antiphon of Tone IV.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`I shall commemorate thy name * in every generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, and incline thine ear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(1:39-49, 56)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:1,verses:`39-49, 56`},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`Rejoice now, O monastery of Kursk! Adorn thyself and dance, O Russian land! For lo! the Queen of heaven herself with a most pure countenance doth dwell in thy midst by her grace, pouring forth her mercies abundantly upon the faithful. Wherefore, she doth hear from all unceasingly: Rejoice, O Theotokos Mary, thou wonder of wonders!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone II`,tone:2},canon_rubric:{text:`The Canon of the Theotokos, in Tone IV, with six Troparia, including the Irmos; the acrostic whereof is: “I dare to offer thee praise, O Theotokos”:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`The Canon of the Theotokos, in Tone IV, with six Troparia, including the Irmos; the acrostic whereof is: “I dare to offer thee praise, O Theotokos”:`,acrostic:`I dare to offer thee praise, O Theotokos`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`I shall open my mouth, * and be filled with the Spirit, * and utter discourse to the Queen and Mother; * and be seen radiantly keeping festival, * joyfully praising her wonders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Disdain not my lowliness, O Theotokos, and compensate for my weakness; sanctify my heart and mind, and open thou my lips, that I may make bold to offer thee a hymn.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With heartfelt faith we honor thy most pure image, and bowing down before it with compunction, as though beholding thee, the Theotokos, in very truth, and shedding drops of tears, we cry aloud: Rejoice, O Mary, full of grace, blessed Mother of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p7-p8 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating the angelic hosts, let us surround thine image with fear and love, magnifying thee, the prototype, together, and calling upon thy most sweet name: Rejoice, O all-immaculate Bride of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, O ye faithful, and let us kiss the holy icon of the Mother of God with love, for she doth pour forth healings therefrom abundantly, and doth work innumerable miracles for those who have recourse to it with faith and love. Wherefore we cry out to the ever-Virgin: Rejoice!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Theotokos, thou living and plentiful fount, * establish in spiritual fellowship those who sing hymns to thee, * and in thy divine glory * grant them crowns of glory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The eyes of our mind rushing headlong into the abyss of the ages, we see there thine icon, O most pure one, shining more brightly than the sun with rays of mercy, illumining thy home, the Russian land, O Theotokos. Wherefore, we cry unto thee: Rejoice, O our protection and defense!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In its bosom the dark oak of Kursk kept the radiant wonder, the most pure icon of the Mother of God, which had been cut in twain by the impious and grew back together through the power of God. Wherefore, recovering it like a great treasure, the Russian people cried out: Rejoice, O our protection and defense!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Whence is this, that the most blessed Mother of God cometh unto us? A spring of living water sprang forth at the place where the image of the Theotokos abode, refreshing the faithful with streams of healing and curing every wound and infirmity. Wherefore, we cry aloud to her who is full of grace: Rejoice, thou true life-bearing fount!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`At the root of a tree was discovered the icon of her who ineffably gave rise to the Tree of life and budded forth for the world the blessed Fruit. Wherefore, now celebrating the feast of its appearance, we cry out to the most pure one: O most blessed Lady, sever our evil passions at the root, implanting in us good habits, setting out a garden of virtues in us, granting us to be partakers of the life of paradise!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`He who sitteth in glory upon the throne of the Godhead, * Jesus the true God, * is come in a swift cloud * and with His sinless hands he hath saved those who cry: * Glory to Thy power, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Today the Church of Russia doth celebrate, adorned in a godly manner with the glory of the newly-revealed icon of the Theotokos; and chanting divinely beauteous hymns, it calleth to all the faithful, saying: Come, let us rejoice in the Mother of our God, and let us bow down before her precious image, through which the most pure Virgin doth richly bestow gifts of grace upon the Christian people who cry aloud: Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O chosen one of the Mother of God, venerable Father seraphim, ever-vigilant intercessor for the Russian land, thou seest our fervent eagerness, thou hearest the entreaties we offer up before the most pure icon, through which, as a grievously suffering child, thou wast granted healing. Wherefore, stand thou with us, lifting up thy venerable hands, and cry out on our behalf to the Theotokos, that for thy sake she may be well pleased to accept our prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy divine power thou didst confound the mad scheme of the impious atheists to destroy thine icon, O Lady, and didst preserve it unharmed by any destructive action; and while the earth quaked and pillars were cast down, thine icon but turned, averting its face from the vile deeds of men. Wherefore, marveling at this most glorious wonder, we earnestly entreat thee: Turn not thy most pure face away from us, for lo! with contrite hearts we flee to thee and weep, and cry out in compunction: Let not our wickedness prevail over thy tender compassion, but have mercy and save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst preserve thy precious icon unharmed by the hands of the evildoers and cruel atheists who trampled down the holy things of God, and upon thy people didst thou bestow it, which we keep as the apple of our eye. Wherefore, O Lady, do thou ever reveal the sign of thy mercy unto us therein.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`All creation stands in awe of thy divine glory; * for thou, O Virgin who hast not known wedlock, * didst contain within thy womb the God of all, * and gave birth to the timeless Son, * bestowing peace, upon all who hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Let us radiantly celebrate this light-bearing day, whereon a spiritual ray hath shone forth unto the salvation of the world in the nativity of the most pure Bride of God, whereon also the icon of the Theotokos, like the morning star, announcing the day of deliverance, hath appeared to the land of Russia which languished in the darkness of misfortunes and sorrows. Wherefore, we cry to the most blessed one: Rejoice, for thou hast lighted a beacon of hope for us which cannot be extinguished!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Where sin increaseth, there doth the grace of God exceedingly abound. Wherefore, O Lady, look down upon our weakness, see our boundless abasement, but behold also our faith, and hearken to our cry; and hasten thou to assist us who are helpless, illumining us with thy mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us not fear the dark powers of Hades, but having put on the armor of light, let us manfully stand against them, having the all-hymned Theotokos as commander. For lo! she doth mightily war against the enemy, helping the faithful who call upon her most pure name.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We confess thee in truth to be the Theotokos, and we honor the form of thy most pure countenance in an Orthodox manner. We turn away from every sin and vile act; we pray to be granted to do good, and, humbling our souls, we cry: Most holy Theotokos, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Celebrating the divine and solemn feast * of the Mother of God * O ye divinely wise, * let us come, clapping our hands, * and glorify God who was born of her.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Let despondency depart from us, O brethren, and let the showers of adverse thoughts be dispelled by the Spirit of God; for lo! the Mother of God herself doth openly dwell amongst us, worshipped in her wonderworking icon, and shining brighter than the sun in the miracles that proceed therefrom. Wherefore, we cry out from the depths of our hearts: O most holy Lady, ever abide with us in thy grace!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When temptation doth assail us, when we fall into sorrow and pain, when patience doth fail within us and our spirit is troubled, let us make haste to the image of the most holy Virgin and, pouring forth tears, cry out to her from our hearts: Stretch forth thy hands which held God unto us, and lead us up from the abyss of evil!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who didst bear the everlasting Joy of the world, thou art the joy of joys who hast driven away the grief of sin and dost grant our troubled souls divine relief. Cease not thy supplications for the Christian world, for, after God, it is through thee that each is saved and led forth from the depths of offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Lo! the hordes of evil demons that besiege Christians stand far off, watching, not daring to approach, fearing the glory of the icon of the Theotokos, which burneth the vile demons, but doth mightily aid the faithful, protecting them from all enemies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Refusing to worship created things * in place of the Creator, * the divinely wise youths bravely trampled down the threatening fire * and rejoicing they sang aloud: * O supremely hymned Lord and God of our Fathers, Blessed art Thou.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The angels in thy service revere thee, the seraphim glorify thee in fear, O Theotokos; and how can we who dwell on earth dare to hymn thee with our impure lips? Yet we hope in thy mercy, and through thee unceasingly cry out to the Master and Creator of all: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ, accept Thy most pure Mother whom Thou hast given us as a help and who now doth fervently pray for us, that having attained unto life everlasting through her intercessions, we may cry aloud with all who have obtained salvation: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, Who callest Thy Mother blessed, be Thou entreated by her intercessions, and may the light of Thy countenance be signed upon us, that, rising from the sleep of sin, we may piously begin to walk towards the day, unceasingly crying out in our hearts: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating the children in Babylon, let us not bow down before the golden image of man-pleasing and Mammon, but let us venerate the image of the immaculate Mother of our God and, filled with heavenly joy, let us cry out to Christ, the Benefactor of all: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Offspring of the Theotokos * saved the holy children in the furnace. * He who was then prefigured hath now been born on earth, * and He gathereth all creation to hymn thee: * all ye works praise ye the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With unceasing voices the seraphim hymn thee, O ever-Virgin; the choirs of the saints know not their fill of thy praises; all creation doth glorify thee without ceasing. And shall we alone remain silent? Yet, daring to hope on thy mercy, though unworthy, we glorify thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`All creatures shall in no wise cease to rejoice in thee, O Theotokos; for lo! as the apostle hath said, tongues may cease and knowledge vanish away, but love never faileth. Wherefore, throughout all ages they shall chant praises offered to thee in love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Tell us, O most pure one, what fitting praise can our infirmity offer thee? With what eyes dare we gaze upon thy precious image? Yet, as thou art good, disdain not now our hymns, and in the land of our earthly sojourn reveal to us the form of thy most radiant countenance, that we may glorify thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Surrounding thine ever-adored image in fear and love, O Sovereign Lady, laying aside all earthly cares and raising our spiritual eyes to the heavens, we taste the sweetness of paradise aforetime, which do thou grant us to enjoy that, obtaining everlasting life and salvation, we may joyfully hymn thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Let every mortal born on earth, * radiant with light, in spirit leap for joy; * and let the host of the angelic powers * celebrate and honor the holy feast of the Mother of God, * and let them cry aloud: * Rejoice! O all-blessed Theotokos, * thou pure Ever-virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O all-hymned Virgin, accept our hymns as thy Son did the widow’s mite, and grant us ever to offer them to thee, guiding our life in the world and granting remission of sins, that entering the heavenly mansions through thee, we may magnify thy loving-kindness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let those who do not confess thee to be the Theotokos and who do not honor thine icons be everlastingly put to shame; but let the faithful rejoice in thee. Let the Russian land be thine abode as of old; let holy monasteries abound and churches be beautifully adorned; and let the people be sanctified, that they may celebrate with gladness, magnifying thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Theotokos, our Queen, standing at the right hand of Christ God in the Kingdom of heaven, establish thou a Christian kingdom on earth, setting at naught the counsels of the impious and strengthening faith and piety, that all who dwell on earth may magnify thee with one mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Have we offered thee a worthy hymn, O Lady? Have we glorified thy precious icon as is due? For we know that even hymns a thousand-fold do not suffice for thy glorification, O Virgin. For if we hearken to the fervor of our hearts, our hymns should only be beginning. What, therefore, shall we do? We are at a loss and are in doubt. We glorify the sign of thy mercy, yet with never silent lips and heartfelt love we ever hymn and magnify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`What feast is more radiant or more beautiful than those of the most pure Mother of God? And what name, apart from the name of sweetest Jesus, is more sweet than the name of Mary? For lo! surpassing all the choirs of angels in purity and glory, resplendent as the Mother of the Almighty, she embraceth the whole world, saving sinners and leading the righteous to the heavenly mansions, she casteth down enemies and most gloriously crusheth the head of the serpent. Wherefore, we cry out to her: Every creature doth rejoice in thee, O thou who art full of grace! Glory be to thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy icon, in Tone VII`,tone:7}],exapostilarion:{text:`O Virgin Theotokos, thou most radiant sun, kindle the inextinguishable beacon of the faith of Christ in our land by thy grace, that thereby light may be cast upon darkness and the hearts of the faithful may rejoice therein, giving thanks to Christ, the Lover of mankind, and granting to all great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy icon, in Tone III`,tone:3},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`By my sins have I put aside the robe of baptism. How can I enter in unto the banquet of the Lord, having no wedding garment, if thou, O Theotokos, dost not cover me with thy mantle and utter a word to the King of glory on my behalf, wretch that I am? Wherefore, placing my hope on thee alone, I stretch forth my hands to thee: Do thou hearken, and protect and help me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Exapostilarion Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone III`,tone:3},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the holy icon, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Bowing the knee of our hearts, and lifting up our eyes to the holy hill, let us fall down before the face of the most pure Theotokos, confessing our weakness, asking her all-powerful aid, and commending our life to her fervent intercession. For we believe that she who hath wiped every tear from the face of the earth will not reject our entreaty.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,repeat:2},{text:`What hymns shall we sing to thee, O Theotokos? What gifts shall we offer thee? Thou beholdest our spiritual poverty. Yet accept thou our teardrops as a pearl of great price, and our prayer and heartfelt sighing as incense; and turn thou our grief into joy, for thou art the most sweet consolation of the faithful!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`All things are possible for thee when thou prayest to thy Son and God, O Lady; and none can stand against thy maternal boldness, for there is no sin that doth vanquish thy tender compassion. Wherefore, we flee to thy mighty protection, hoping on thy most powerful intercession; and, after God, we commend ourselves, each other and all our life unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises 3`},label:`plain`}],praises_closer:{text:`Pray thou fervently for the whole world, O Theotokos, for it is in need of thine aid, for the snares of the evil one have spread over the face of all the earth, the nations rage and storms of temptations have risen against the Church of God. Wherefore, as once in Cana of Galilee, speak thou a word to thy Son, that He transform the water of temptations and sorrows into the wine of compunction and divine gladness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Praises Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone V`,tone:5}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia, four each from ODES III and VI of the canon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`The eyes of our mind rushing headlong into the abyss of the ages, we see there thine icon, O most pure one, shining more brightly than the sun with rays of mercy, illumining thy home, the Russian land, O Theotokos. Wherefore, we cry unto thee: Rejoice, O our protection and defense!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In its bosom the dark oak of Kursk kept the radiant wonder, the most pure icon of the Mother of God, which had been cut in twain by the impious and grew back together through the power of God. Wherefore, recovering it like a great treasure, the Russian people cried out: Rejoice, O our protection and defense!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Whence is this, that the most blessed Mother of God cometh unto us? A spring of living water sprang forth at the place where the image of the Theotokos abode, refreshing the faithful with streams of healing and curing every wound and infirmity. Wherefore, we cry aloud to her who is full of grace: Rejoice, thou true life-bearing fount!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`At the root of a tree was discovered the icon of her who ineffably gave rise to the Tree of life and budded forth for the world the blessed Fruit. Wherefore, now celebrating the feast of its appearance, we cry out to the most pure one: O most blessed Lady, sever our evil passions at the root, implanting in us good habits, setting out a garden of virtues in us, granting us to be partakers of the life of paradise!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let despondency depart from us, O brethren, and let the showers of adverse thoughts be dispelled by the Spirit of God; for lo! the Mother of God herself doth openly dwell amongst us, worshipped in her wonderworking icon, and shining brighter than the sun in the miracles that proceed therefrom. Wherefore, we cry out from the depths of our hearts: O most holy Lady, ever abide with us in thy grace!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`When temptation doth assail us, when we fall into sorrow and pain, when patience doth fail within us and our spirit is troubled, let us make haste to the image of the most holy Virgin and, pouring forth tears, cry out to her from our hearts: Stretch forth thy hands which held God unto us, and lead us up from the abyss of evil!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who didst bear the everlasting Joy of the world, thou art the joy of joys who hast driven away the grief of sin and dost grant our troubled souls divine relief. Cease not thy supplications for the Christian world, for, after God, it is through thee that each is saved and led forth from the depths of offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 7`},label:`plain`},{text:`Lo! the hordes of evil demons that besiege Christians stand far off, watching, not daring to approach, fearing the glory of the icon of the Theotokos, which burneth the vile demons, but doth mightily aid the faithful, protecting them from all enemies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Beatitude 8`},label:`plain`}],prokeimenon:{text:`My soul doth magnify the Lord, * and my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Savior.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},tone:3,sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone III: The hymn of the Theotokos`,label_inline:!0},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`For He hath looked upon the lowliness of His handmaiden; for behold, from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`THE EPISTLE OF PAUL TO THE HEBREWS`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(9:1-7)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:9,verses:`1-7`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, and incline thine ear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VIII`,label_inline:!0,tone:8},alleluia_verse:{text:`The rich among the people shall entreat thy countenance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(10:38-42; 11:27-28)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:10,verses:`10:38-42, 11:27-28`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`I shall receive the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-08A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"09-27":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYR CALLISTRATUS & HIS COMPANIONS`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 27th DAY OF THE MONTH OF SEPTEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`09-27.pdf`,note:`OVERLAP DATE for the V1/V2 comparison (menaion_v2_wirein_spec.md section 5). ODS 3rd ed. vol. III has no entry for 27 September. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera at Lord I have cried and a Glory of the saints, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology, no aposticha printed: Simple, Fekula 2A, agreeing with V1. TWO kontakia in Tone IV, after Ode III and after Ode VI (with the Ikos), both printed again at Liturgy: positional lists, no entry-level canonical kontakion. AT LITURGY prints only the troparion and the two kontakia.`,troparion:{text:`In their sufferings, Thy martyrs O Lord, * received imperishable crowns from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * they set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By their supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 Troparion of the holy martyrs`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p1 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p6 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,tone:4},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy martyrs, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O martyred spiritual athlete Callistratus, * with thy mind illumined * by the light of piety, * thou didst unwaveringly tread the path * which leadeth to heavenly blessedness, * having vanquished all the wiles of the adversary. * Wherefore, we praise thee, * honoring thy sacred memory, ** O most blessed one.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O divinely wise martyr Callistratus, * enriched by the words of life, * thou didst guide unto life * those who before were dead in accursedness through ignorance; * and, thou didst die with great zeal, O glorious one, * for they who believe in Christ, Who is the resurrection of us all, * most truly dwell in Him. * With them remember us ** to the supremely good Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O sacred martyr Gymnasius, * beheaded by the sword, * thou didst truly drown the Pharaoh of delusion * in the torrent of thy blood; * and now thou pourest forth healings upon all * who have recourse to thy temple with faith, * and therein praise thy struggles, * and celebrate thine honored memory, ** O blessed one.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Before Thy precious Cross, death was terrifying to mortals; but after Thy glorious Passion, mortals were terrifying to death. Thus the spiritual athlete was able to abolish all the power of the enemy: Through his supplications save our souls, O Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},composer:`Byzantius`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of Byzantius, in Tone IV`,tone:4},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon beholding Thee, * the Lamb and Shepherd, upon the Tree, * the ewe-lamb who bore Thee lamented, * and maternally exclaimed to Thee: * “O most desired Son, * how is it that Thou art suspended upon the tree of the Cross? * How is it that Thine arms and legs are nailed * by the iniquitous ones, O long-suffering Word, ** and that Thou hast shed Thy blood, O Master?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`kontakia_ode3`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakia_ode6`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, with 8 Troparia; and that of the martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the composition of Joseph, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, with 8 Troparia; and that of the martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the composition of Joseph, in Tone VIII:`,composer:`Joseph`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us, O ye people, send up a hymn * unto our wondrous God * Who hath freed Israel from bondage, * chanting a hymn of victory * and crying aloud: * We sing unto Thee, O only Master.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Walking the path of suffering without faltering, for the lost thou didst become a path leading to places of divine repose, O blessed one; wherefore, having assembled, we praise thee with faith, O Callistratus.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shining forth like a most radiant star, thou hast illumined the Church of Christ with the light of divine knowledge; and driving away the darkness of ignorance, O martyr, thou didst topple the ruined temples of falsehood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Patiently enduring every trial, O Callistratus, thou didst not refuse to die for the Life of all; wherefore, rejoicing, thou hast passed over to immortal rest, and dwellest with the angelic choirs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The sacred Gymnasius was shown to be an ember burning with the fire of the divine Spirit; utterly consuming the dross of falsehood, and bedewing with miracles those burning with the heat of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Alone among women, thou didst supra-naturally give birth to One of the Trinity, O all-immaculate one, not having known man; wherefore, we glorify thee and Him Who was born of thee in a manner transcending all cause and all telling.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who established the heavens by Thy word * and founded the earth upon the multitude of waters, * establish me unto the hymning of * Thy glorification O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Refusing to offer any sacrifice unto graven deities, thou didst offer thyself as a pure sacrifice to the God of all Who was sacrificed for us, O martyred spiritual athlete Callistratus.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Arrayed in a purple robe dyed with thy truly sacred blood, O blessed martyr, thou standest, crowned, before the King of ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The enemy was shown to be stripped naked by the divine glory of thee and the spiritual athletes who with thee were clothed from on high, O valiant minded martyr Gymnasius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Earnestly make supplication to thy Son, O Virgin, that He save us from the coming tribulations and from everlasting torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, I have heard the mystery of Thy dispensation; * I have considered Thy works, * and I have glorified Thy Divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Arming thyself against the persecutor like a most excellent commander, O martyr, thou didst lure to divine life those made captive of old, and didst capture them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the showers of thy words thou hast watered the hearts of all, and guided them to the water of everlasting life, O right wondrous spiritual athlete of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The ever-memorable Callistratus is slaughtered like a lamb, his most zealous soldiers having been slain like lambs before him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like a vine, O martyr Gymnasius, through the account of thy suffering thou didst produce ripe grapes, pouring forth the wine of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O maiden, cleanse thou my heart which hath been defiled by the passions, and make it a receptacle of the pure and divine radiance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Thou hast enlightened * with the knowledge of God * the ends of the universe * that lay in the night of ignorance, * do Thou also, O Lord, illumine me * with the dawning of Thy love for mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Loving Christ our God most ardently, O martyr, thou didst suffer, and destroyed the feeble strength of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast shown to be the leader of divine recruits, O martyr Callistratus, and, rejoicing, hast now been enlisted in the armies of the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adorned with the glory of the splendor of martyrdom, O Gymnasius, rejoicing, thou hast now passed over to the splendors of the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast shown to be the east of the Sun of righteousness, O all-immaculate one. Him do thou entreat, that He save those who glorify thee in purity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Cleanse me, O Savior, * for many are mine iniquities; * lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee, * for unto Thee have I cried, * and Thou hast hearkened unto me, * O God of my salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst break the jaws of invisible lions, O wise one, and didst show those who were devoured by the enemy to be partakers of immaterial sweetness, O martyr Callistratus.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Delivering a beautiful and divine discourse concerning God, O most glorious Callistratus, thou didst reveal those who before had wretchedly worshiped inanimate gods, to be divine, and didst suffer with them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Bowing your necks before Christ, O martyrs, ye accepted slaughter and offered yourselves to God as perfect sacrifices; and ye have adorned the Church of the firstborn.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sanctify my mind and illumine my heart, O pure Mother of God, and deliver me from the evils which beset me, that I may glorify thee, O Ever-virgin Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The children of Judaea, * who of old came to dwell in Babylon, * trampled underfoot the flame of the furnace * through their faith in the Trinity, * as they sang: ‘O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Made lustrous as gold by the fire of torments, thou wast shown to be a symbol of the sufferings of Christ, O glorious one, and hast now been laid up in the treasury of God, crying aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by sufferings, thou didst show thyself to be a heaven-forged sword, O Callistratus, cutting down hordes of invisible demons and crying aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast revealed as strong against impiety by the might of the Trinity, O Callistratus; and, illumined with the effulgence thereof, thou dost now cry aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Loving Christ with a steadfast mind, O divinely inspired martyr Gymnasius, thou wast slain with all thy fellow zealots, chanting in thanksgiving: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely joyous one, entreat Him Who was incarnate of thee in a manner past understanding and all telling, that we be saved who honor thee with love and cry out together: O God of .our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Treading down the fiery flame in the furnace, * the divinely eloquent children sang: * ‘Bless the Lord, ye works of the Lord’.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Uprooting the thorns of falsehood, thou didst show thyself to be a most comely garden of paradise, O martyr, producing fruits of piety through divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Looking to the expectations to come in perfect hope, thou didst set thyself apart for struggles, and, emerging triumphant, wast lawfully crowned, O Callistratus.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Acquiring the healing of thy temple, O glorious Gymnasius, those who piously have recourse to it are delivered from evils, praising thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`In that thou art more exalted than all creatures, O divinely joyous and all-immaculate maiden, exalt my mind above the temptations of the deceiver.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Every ear is awestruck at hearing of God’s ineffable condescension, * for the Most High voluntarily descended and assumed flesh, * becoming man in the Virgin’s womb; * wherefore we the faithful magnify the most pure Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The shrine of thy relics poureth forth healing upon all in need, O martyr Callistratus: truly halting illnesses difficult to cure, and dispelling the darkness of evil spirits through the activity, power and grace of the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Bound one to another by grace, O martyrs of Christ, ye were shown to be like a divinely fashioned chain leading up on high and sanctifying the earth with the shedding of your blood. Wherefore, we faithfully celebrate your memory in gladness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With those who suffered with thee thou hast manifestly received an imperishable crown, everlasting glory and gladness, never-ending joy and the heavenly kingdom, O divinely wise Callistratus. With them remember us to the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shining forth today more brightly than the sun, the divine memory of the wise Callistratus, Gymnasius and those who suffered with them illumineth the ends of the earth with radiant brilliance. Through their supplications, O Christ, free us from condemnation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`With gladsome mind we cry out to thee with the voice of Gabriel: Rejoice, O joy of the faithful! Rejoice, O golden lampstand, table, mountain and noetic gate! Rejoice, O divine chariot of Christ the King! Rejoice, O all-blessed one, thou loosing of the curse!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`The Church, making every effort today, * doth offer up mystic praise for those who suffered for her, ** O holy and divine martyrs, right victorious and all-wise.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Kontakion of the holy martyrs (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared ...`,tone:4}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`O ye faithful, let us praise the sufferings of Callistratus, let us hymn the pangs of Gymnasius, and with love let us bless those who suffered patiently with them; and let us cry out to them: O warriors of piety, ask that we be given peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone V`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word ...`,tone:5},{text:`Quickly heal my much suffering soul of the passions, * and my flesh of its infirmities. * Establish my mind in firmness, O most immaculate one, * and grant me quietude of thought, * that I may offer pure prayers to the King of all O Theotokos, ** and ask for the remission of sins.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone V`,tone:5},{text:`Beholding Thee suspended on the Cross between two thieves of Thine own will, O Christ, Thy Mother, her womb rent asunder maternally, said: “O my sinless Son, how is it that Thou art unjustly nailed to the Cross like a malefactor, desiring to give life to the human race, in that Thou art compassionate?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],kontakia_ode6:[{text:`Having endured multifarious wounds * and manifestly received crowns from God, * pray to Christ for us who celebrate your most festive memorial, * O great Callistratus * and ye blessed ones who suffered with him, * that He may grant peace to His flock and people; ** for He is the confirmation of the faithful.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Kontakion of the holy martyrs (after Ode VI)`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Having been lifted up on the Cross ...`,tone:4},{text:`Gazing upon the shrine of thy relics, O Callistratus, I hymn and magnify the pangs and sufferings which thou didst suffer. Wherefore, I beseech thee: Render Christ, the Judge of thy contest, merciful to me, that by grace He grant me utterance with divine words, that I may be able to praise thy struggles; for no man is able to recount thy mighty deeds; how thou didst manfully enter the tribunal, denouncing the wicked thoughts of the tyrants. Christ is the confirmation of the faithful!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ikos`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`O the wonder! How have those who are clay by nature been shown to be golden? For neither fire, nor the sword, nor the teeth of wild beasts, nor tortures, nor wounds destroyed them; and, having cast down the incorporeal one with their flesh, they pray for us to the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy martyrs`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Rejoice, O palace of God! Rejoice, O mountain densely wooded! Rejoice, O divine table! Rejoice, bush unburnt! Rejoice, throne of glory! Rejoice, golden jar! Rejoice, most radiant lamp! Rejoice, O Mary, Virgin Mother, thou light cloud!`,tier:1,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakia`],kontakia:[{text:`The Church, making every effort today, * doth offer up mystic praise for those who suffered for her, ** O holy and divine martyrs, right victorious and all-wise.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Kontakion of Ode III at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`ODE III, Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Having endured multifarious wounds * and manifestly received crowns from God, * pray to Christ for us who celebrate your most festive memorial, * O great Callistratus * and ye blessed ones who suffered with him, * that He may grant peace to His flock and people; ** for He is the confirmation of the faithful.`,tier:2,src:{file:`09-27.pdf`,locus:`p6 Kontakion of Ode VI at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`ODE VI, Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,tone:4}]}}]}};export{e as default};